{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\jeffr\\\\.codex\\\\skills\\\\roundtable\\\\SKILL.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\jeffr\\\\.codex\\\\skills\\\\roundtable\\\\SKILL.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: roundtable\ndescription: Automated OpenRouter model roundtable for hardening plans, specs, architecture docs, sprint plans, and problem statements; use for /roundtable, panel review, round-robin, pressure-test, or make this bulletproof requests.\nversion: 1.1.0\n---\n\n# Roundtable\n\nHarden a document by combining Codex's grounded repo review with independent\nfrontier-model critiques through OpenRouter. The panel proposes; Codex disposes.\nNever outsource synthesis to a panel model.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when the user asks for `/roundtable`, a roundtable, a panel,\nother models' opinions, a round-robin, a pressure test, or to make a plan/spec\nbulletproof. Prefer [kibitz](skill:kibitz) instead when the user specifically\nwants local CLI agents such as Claude Code, Antigravity, and Codex to read the\nrepo directly.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` in the environment, or on Windows in `HKCU\\Environment`.\n  The script reads both. Never pass the key on the command line.\n- A document to harden, usually Markdown.\n- Grounding artifacts when the topic touches code: real source files, workflow\n  JSON, schemas, logs, or docs. Panel claims are hypotheses until Codex verifies\n  them against these artifacts.\n\n## OTR Defaults\n\nFor the OldTimeRadio repo, follow the repo's standing shape:\n\n- Panel size: 2-3 model families by default.\n- Default roster: GPT + Gemini + Tencent Hy3 free.\n- Hy3 model: `tencent/hy3:free`, released July 6, 2026, 262K context, free on\n  OpenRouter at install time. Current public reports say the free promo lasts\n  through July 21, 2026; verify with `--list-models` or the OpenRouter page if\n  cost matters.\n- Hy3 is configured with high reasoning and a larger output cap in\n  [panel.config.json](assets/panel.config.json), so the free lane is used hard\n  while the paid GPT/Gemini lanes stay controlled.\n- Optional fourth lane: add `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro` or `x-ai/grok-4.3` only\n  when the user explicitly asks for extra diversity or the problem is genuinely\n  unresolved after the normal panel.\n\n## The 4-Round Arc\n\nRun all four rounds unless the user explicitly asks for a single pass.\n\n| Round | Focus | Review prompt |\n|-------|-------|---------------|\n| R1 | High-level arc / creative coherence | [review-prompt-r1.md](references/review-prompt-r1.md) |\n| R2 | Coding plan / implementability | [review-prompt-r2.md](references/review-prompt-r2.md) |\n| R3 | Wiring / integration / sequencing | [review-prompt-r3.md](references/review-prompt-r3.md) |\n| R4 | Convergence / residual defects | [review-prompt-r4.md](references/review-prompt-r4.md) |\n\nRead [synthesis-prompt.md](references/synthesis-prompt.md) before judging and\nsynthesizing a pass.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Set up `docs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<topic>/roundtable/`. Save the starting document as\n   `pass00_plan.md`.\n2. Codex writes `pass<NN>/codex_anchor.md`: a grounded VERDICT / MUST-FIX /\n   SHOULD-FIX review in the same format as that round's prompt.\n3. Run [roundtable_pass.py](scripts/roundtable_pass.py) live. Do not do a\n   cost-estimate-only dry run for normal OTR use.\n4. Ground every panel claim against the real files. Label each claim CONFIRMED,\n   MISREAD, or UNVERIFIABLE. Discard misreads and hallucinations.\n5. Synthesize as Codex only. Save `pass<NN>_plan.md` and\n   `pass<NN>_judgment.md`.\n6. Advance R1 -> R2 -> R3 -> R4. After R4, deliver the final hardened plan,\n   judgment log, raw review locations, verify-at-build items, and total spend.\n\n## Calling the Fan-Out Script\n\nThe script performs exactly one OpenRouter pass and writes one review per model.\n\n```powershell\nC:\\Users\\jeffr\\Documents\\ComfyUI\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe `\n  C:\\Users\\jeffr\\.codex\\skills\\roundtable\\scripts\\roundtable_pass.py `\n  --doc docs\\<date>-<topic>\\roundtable\\pass<NN>_plan.md `\n  --out docs\\<date>-<topic>\\roundtable\\pass<NN> `\n  --config C:\\Users\\jeffr\\.codex\\skills\\roundtable\\assets\\panel.config.json `\n  --prompt C:\\Users\\jeffr\\.codex\\skills\\roundtable\\references\\review-prompt-r1.md `\n  --grounding nodes\\the_real_file.py workflows\\otr_scifi_16gb_full.json `\n  --budget 5.00\n```\n\nUseful flags:\n\n- `--models a/b,c/d` overrides the roster for one pass.\n- `--max-tokens`, `--temperature`, and `--reasoning-effort` override config\n  defaults for every model in that pass.\n- `--list-models` prints the current OpenRouter catalog and pricing.\n- `--dry-run` exists for script validation, but the OTR operating rule is to run\n  live when the user asks for a roundtable.\n\n## Cost Discipline\n\n- The script has a hard `--budget` ceiling and refuses to start if known\n  worst-case panel cost exceeds it.\n- It prints `Actual spend this pass: ~$X.XXXX` after every live run, including\n  `$0.0000` for an all-free pass with known zero pricing.\n- Accumulate pass spend and report the total after R4.\n- Do not add rounds past R4 unless the user asks or a material unresolved split\n  remains.\n\n## Conventions\n\nWrite artifacts as UTF-8 with no BOM, ASCII where practical. Keep roundtable\nhistory under `docs/<date>-<topic>/roundtable/`. Never present an ungrounded\npanel claim as fact.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
