{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r4\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$n=0;$n -lt 240;$n++){ '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f (\"'$n+1),$lines[$n] }'","aggregated_output":"    1: # dynamic_story -- Story-Derived Visual Direction: Scoped Design (docs-only)\r\n    2: \r\n    3: Date: 2026-07-12 (rev 4 -- r1 arc + r2 coding plan + r3 wiring, each hardened by\r\n    4: a kibitz round: codex gpt-5.6-sol @ ultra + antigravity gemini-3.5-pro; driver\r\n    5: anchors, panel reviews and judgments in\r\n    6: kibitz-runs/2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual/{r1,r2,r3}/)\r\n    7: Author: Claude (Cowork), docs-only architecture owner for this feature.\r\n    8: Implementation owner: Codex (all code, tests, registries, prompts, workflow JSON).\r\n    9: Status: DESIGN ONLY. Nothing in this document is implemented. No code, test,\r\n   10: prompt, registry, or workflows/otr_canonical.json change accompanies it.\r\n   11: \r\n   12: Scope contract honored here:\r\n   13: \r\n   14: - One additional option (`dynamic_story`) in the EXISTING visual-style dropdown.\r\n   15: - When selected, an LLM reads the final accepted/frozen story and authors an\r\n   16:   episode-specific, evidence-bound `visual_direction` artifact that every\r\n   17:   downstream visual composer consumes.\r\n   18: - An explicit user-selected named visual pack keeps current behavior,\r\n   19:   byte-identical, and always wins. `dynamic_story` is opt-in per episode.\r\n   20: \r\n   21: Every code claim below is grounded `file:line` against the real Windows repo\r\n   22: (v2.0-alpha working tree, 2026-07-12). This design is GRADED against\r\n   23: docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md; the lesson each requirement discharges is\r\n   24: named inline.\r\n   25: \r\n   26: ---\r\n   27: \r\n   28: ## 1. Grounded current dataflow (what exists today)\r\n   29: \r\n   30: ### 1.1 The visual-style selector and its one stamping point\r\n   31: \r\n   32: - The dropdown lives on OTR_LedgerScriptWriter: choices come LIVE from the\r\n   33:   visual-style pack registry (`list_style_ids()`) at INPUT_TYPES\r\n   34:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:2871-2889), default `sci_fi_radio`.\r\n   35: - The id is gated fail-loud at the top of `run()` beside the source-bank gate:\r\n   36:   `_otr_visual_styles.resolve_visual_style(visual_style)` -- unknown id raises\r\n   37:   `UnknownVisualStyleError` before ANY story work\r\n   38:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3334-3339).\r\n   39: - The ONE authoritative stamp: `meta[\"visual_style\"] = resolved[\"visual_style\"]`\r\n   40:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3651-3655). The comment there is the\r\n   41:   threading law: \"every downstream visual composer reads meta['visual_style']\r\n   42:   via get_visual_style(meta) off the serialized ledger\".\r\n   43: - Channel separation is explicit and load-bearing: `meta.style` is the STORY\r\n   44:   grammar slug, `meta.visual_style` is the visual prompt-pack selector; the two\r\n   45:   are never crossed (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:216-222, 2249-2261).\r\n   46: - The dropdown surface is TEST-PINNED to the registry:\r\n   47:   `test_choices_are_exactly_the_registry` asserts\r\n   48:   `choices == list(vs.list_style_ids())`\r\n   49:   (tests/test_visual_style_widget_3c.py:62-66), and `visual_style` is\r\n   50:   positionally pinned at INPUT_TYPES index 24 (:54-60) and at\r\n   51:   `widgets_values[24] == \"sci_fi_radio\"` in the canonical workflow.\r\n   52: \r\n   53: ### 1.2 The pack registry (the resolution seam dynamic_story must enter through)\r\n   54: \r\n   55: - Packs are JSON files under `nodes/visual_styles/<style_id>.json`; the module\r\n   56:   is pure behavior, lazy, fail-loud (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:3-13, 50).\r\n   57: - `DEFAULT_STYLE_ID = \"sci_fi_radio\"` (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:53).\r\n   58: - Schema v2 is a FIXED field inventory: v1 fields (style_id, label, the four\r\n   59:   tails, forbidden_terms, ...) + 11 required look/subject strings + 4 dict\r\n   60:   fields with exact key sets (open_subjects, motion_registers,\r\n   61:   still_word_typography, still_word_backdrop)\r\n   62:   (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:60-102). Validation is strict: template\r\n   63:   placeholder rules, mouth-vocabulary contract, 240-char motion budget,\r\n   64:   forbidden-terms lint (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:109-123, 184+).\r\n   65: - Resolution: `resolve_visual_style(style_id)` -- unknown id = hard error, no\r\n   66:   fallback (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:367-375); `get_visual_style(meta)` --\r\n   67:   absent/empty `meta[\"visual_style\"]` = production default; PRESENT-but-unknown\r\n   68:   fails LOUD (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:378-390). Both are META-ONLY seams --\r\n   69:   they never see `lines`/`cast` (r1 finding; drives 5.3).\r\n   70: - The loaded packs are CACHED module-globally (`_STYLES`,\r\n   71:   nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:170, 355-359). A per-episode dynamic pack must\r\n   72:   NEVER enter that cache.\r\n   73: - The geometry-vs-look law (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:7-9): packs own ONLY\r\n   74:   look/subject vocabulary; framing/headroom/mouth-safety GEOMETRY stays in\r\n   75:   Python. `dynamic_story` obeys the same law -- and the LLM does not even author\r\n   76:   every pack LOOK field (2.4).\r\n   77: \r\n   78: ### 1.3 The story freeze boundary (what \"final accepted story\" means)\r\n   79: \r\n   80: - OTR_LedgerScriptWriter -> OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade; Phase 10 runs the\r\n   81:   deterministic gap audit and, on success, stamps `meta.cleanup_locked = True`,\r\n   82:   `meta.freeze_timestamp` (ISO-8601 UTC), and `meta.freeze_verdict =\r\n   83:   frozen_clean | frozen_with_warns` (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:758-819,\r\n   84:   stamps at 806-811). Critical gaps raise `FreezeAssertionError` and stamp\r\n   85:   `needs_full_rerun` (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:787-795).\r\n   86: - Freeze locks story CONTENT, not the whole rows. OTR_CastLock assigns voice\r\n   87:   presets AFTER the freeze (acknowledged inside the freeze audit itself,\r\n   88:   nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:493-502); OTR_ShotLock overlays per-line audio\r\n   89:   timing IN PLACE (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:169-221) and stamps a whole\r\n   90:   `ledger['video']` section + `meta.video_revision` (:1104-1131). Consequence:\r\n   91:   the RAW `lines`/`cast` arrays are NOT stable post-freeze -- any staleness check\r\n   92:   must hash an authored-content DTO, never the raw rows (2.5).\r\n   93: - The cascade unloads a locally-resident writer LLM in a `finally` block and\r\n   94:   stamps `meta.freeze_unload_ok` (nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:377-387,\r\n   95:   453-478). That receipt is a PRECONDITION for this feature (5.2): a resident\r\n   96:   writer LLM plus a fresh creative LLM is an OOM on a 16 GB card.\r\n   97: - **There is NO top-level `beats` array.** Beats are DERIVED from lines inside\r\n   98:   ShotLock, with `beat_id = line_id` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:260-288), and the\r\n   99:   synthetic opening-music beat `OPENING_MUSIC_BEAT_ID = \"b000_music_open\"` is\r\n  100:   created LATER still, by `derive_opening_music_beat(ledger, fps)` (:291-301).\r\n  101:   Nothing keyed to a beat exists at direction time.\r\n  102: \r\n  103: ### 1.4 Canonical wiring (workflows/otr_canonical.json, live graph)\r\n  104: \r\n  105: Read out of the real file: `last_node_id = 95`, `last_link_id = 283`, 23 nodes,\r\n  106: 57 links, `groups: []` (empty -- no bounding box constrains placement), every\r\n  107: node `mode == 0` (nothing muted).\r\n  108: \r\n  109: - Writer (node 1) `script_json` -> link 230 -> FreezeCascade (node 62).\r\n  110:   `visual_style` is combined widget slot 24 (`widgets_values[24] ==\r\n  111:   \"sci_fi_radio\"`; `inputs[24]` carries `\"widget\": {\"name\": \"visual_style\"}`\r\n  112:   with `link: null` -- the widget-as-input serialization, not a forceInput).\r\n  113:   The 34-entry vector is APPEND-ONLY (BUG-LOCAL-097); this feature does not\r\n  114:   touch it.\r\n  115: - **FreezeCascade (62) out[1] `script_json` fans out to SIX links:**\r\n  116:   `[16, 231, 232, 233, 252, 255]` --\r\n  117:   `[16, 62, 1, 12, 2]` -> OTR_SignalLostVideo (12);\r\n  118:   `[231, 62, 1, 81, 0]` -> OTR_BatchCharacterVoices (81);\r\n  119:   `[232, 62, 1, 82, 0]` -> OTR_AnnouncerVoice (82);\r\n  120:   `[233, 62, 1, 83, 0]` -> OTR_StableAudioTheme (83);\r\n  121:   `[252, 62, 1, 90, 0]` -> OTR_ShotLock (90);\r\n  122:   `[255, 62, 1, 89, 0]` -> OTR_MetaBriefImagePromptGen (89).\r\n  123:   Only 252 and 255 are the VISUAL-lane consumers. **16 / 231 / 232 / 233 MUST\r\n  124:   keep reading the RAW freeze json** -- the audio trio is pinned to it by\r\n  125:   tests/test_full_workflow_v2_audio_wiring.py:220-232, and node 80 OTR_CastLock\r\n  126:   keeps sourcing 62.out[6] (`v2_ledger_json`, link 234). The direction node is\r\n  127:   inserted in the VISUAL lane ONLY.\r\n  128: - OTR_VideoDirector (87) -> link 270 -> OTR_ImageDirector (88) in[0]; -> link\r\n  129:   251 -> ShotLock in[2]. ImageDirector -> link 254 -> MetaBrief in[1]; -> link\r\n  130:   257 -> OTR_ImageGenDispatcher (91) in[1]. MetaBrief out[0] -> link 258 ->\r\n  131:   Dispatcher in[2]. ShotLock out[0] -> link 256 -> Dispatcher in[0]; out[4]\r\n  132:   `episode_id` -> link 268 -> Dispatcher in[4]. OTR_EpisodeAssembler (7) out[3]\r\n  133:   `audio_done` -> link 253 -> ShotLock in[1] and -> link 259 -> Dispatcher\r\n  134:   gate_in. Dispatcher out[0] -> link 260 -> OTR_VideoRenderBatch (92) in[0];\r\n  135:   out[1] `image_done` -> link 267 -> RenderBatch in[2].\r\n  136: - Node 89: `widgets_values [False]`; inputs `script_json`(255),\r\n  137:   `image_policy_json`(254), `gate_in`(null), `consistency_gate_warn_only`(widget).\r\n  138:   Node 90: `widgets_values [False]`; inputs `script_json`(252),\r\n  139:   `audio_done`(253), `video_policy_json`(251), `image_done`(null),\r\n  140:   `gate_in`(null), `consistency_gate_warn_only`(widget); **its `done` output\r\n  141:   (out[3]) ships UNWIRED (`links: []`)** -- the precedent for the new node's own\r\n  142:   unwired `done`.\r\n  143: - Free placement rectangle for a new node: x 1060-1440, y 760-1000 is empty\r\n  144:   (62 is at x 620; 89 at x 1080 y 1040; 90 at x 1129 y 1200; 91 at x 1560).\r\n  145: \r\n  146: The Dispatcher receives its ledger via ShotLock's whole-ledger re-serialization\r\n  147: (parse at nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1040, re-emit at :1142), so a meta artifact\r\n  148: stamped upstream reaches it with no extra wire.\r\n  149: \r\n  150: ### 1.5 Where the style is actually consumed (THREE independent resolvers)\r\n  151: \r\n  152: - **Image prompts (MetaBrief).** `derive_image_prompts` resolves the style ONCE\r\n  153:   at entry -- `_vstyle = _resolve_style(meta)` (:1601-1609) -- and threads it\r\n  154:   down. **Its signature takes NO ledger:** `derive_image_prompts(cast, meta, *,\r\n  155:   llm_fn=None, ..., lines=None, ...)` (:1570-1574), and `generate()` parses the\r\n  156:   ledger but passes only `cast` / `meta` / `lines` (:2137-2168). Downstream of\r\n  157:   the threaded pack: portrait fallback + LLM instruction builders (:1148-1238),\r\n  158:   beat-aware character scene builder (:1241-1366), radio-host prompts (:356-444),\r\n  159:   mesh fodder + background plate (:1437-1496), still_word cards (:942-1013), and\r\n  160:   the aspect anchors (:171-188).\r\n  161: - **Video prompts (ShotLock).** Every talking-head prompt is finished through\r\n  162:   `finish_visual_prompt(meta, text_prompt)` -- inside a BARE\r\n  163:   `except Exception: pass` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:626-636), so a style failure\r\n  164:   is silently swallowed today (7.2).\r\n  165: - **Video render (render_driver).** It resolves the style ITSELF:\r\n  166:   `_vstyle = get_visual_style((ledger or {}).get(\"meta\") or {})`\r\n  167:   (nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_driver.py:1248) -- a THIRD resolution point\r\n  168:   that raises on the sentinel -- and one branch builds its prompt core from the\r\n  169:   BRIEF, not the pack: `core = get_story_brief_ltx(_meta)` (:2069) then\r\n  170:   `finish_visual_prompt(...)` (:2080).\r\n  171: - The helper family (`_resolve_style` :330, `get_era_tail` :344,\r\n  172:   `compose_still_prompt` :590, `finish_visual_prompt` :667 in\r\n  173:   nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py) resolves the pack from meta.\r\n  174: - LOOK-AUTHORITY REALITY: the era tail is BRIEF-FIRST -- the brief's\r\n  175:   `atmosphere_line`/`visual_palette`/lighting win, and the pack's `era_tail` is\r\n  176:   only the fallback default (nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:356-370, 401,\r\n  177:   414, 428). A design that authors a new palette in the pack alone would be\r\n  178:   silently shadowed by the brief, in BOTH lanes. 5.4 resolves the precedence.\r\n  179: - ShotLock stamps per-shot `creative` sidecars with `prompt_hash` +\r\n  180:   `request_hash` into `ledger['video'].shots[]` (:637-647, 913-948).\r\n  181: \r\n  182: ### 1.6 Image dispatch, cache, and persistence (the replay substrate)\r\n  183: \r\n  184: - Dispatcher cache key: `request_cache_key(role, object_id, prompt_hash, seed,\r\n  185:   engine_id, engine_version, kind, w, h)` -- \"a change in ANY field -> new key ->\r\n  186:   regen\" (nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:117-129). It keys the PROMPT HASH: a\r\n  187:   change to rationale or a receipt that does not alter a composed prompt does NOT\r\n  188:   invalidate the cache.\r\n  189: - **A cache HIT CLONES the previous row** (`fresh = dict(ref_row or {})`) and\r\n  190:   overwrites only `provenance` (:627-632) -- so any provenance field the design\r\n  191:   adds would be INHERITED STALE on a hit unless it is set explicitly on BOTH\r\n  192:   paths (7.5).\r\n  193: - Results land in `ledger[\"images\"]` and persist via\r\n  194:   `stamp_durable(sections={\"images\": ...})` (:796-826;\r\n  195:   nodes/production_ledger.py:408-422). `OTR_TEST_MODE=1` makes `stamp_durable`\r\n  196:   SKIP the disk write (:408-452; conftest sets it, tests/conftest.py:38).\r\n  197: - **A canonical re-queue is never a replay.** The writer and the cascade both\r\n  198:   return `time.time()` from `IS_CHANGED` (\"always re-execute\",\r\n  199:   nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3023-3028;\r\n  200:   nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:269-272), so re-queuing writes a FRESH story\r\n  201:   and a FRESH freeze. Replay is a test-bench property, not a live-smoke leg (9.3).\r\n  202: \r\n  203: ### 1.7 Ledger save/merge ownership (what survives, what gets dropped)\r\n  204: \r\n  205: `Ledger.save()` merges in-memory state with the on-disk ledger\r\n  206: (nodes/production_ledger.py:1287-1346, 1357-1513):\r\n  207: \r\n  208: - TOP-LEVEL: only `TOP_PRESERVE = (schema_version, audio_gates, transitions,\r\n  209:   radio_bookend_path)` is copied forward (:1387-1393). An unknown top-level key\r\n  210:   absent from a later in-memory save is DROPPED. Top-level is NOT ledger-safe.\r\n  211: - META: per-key merge -- disk wins only where in-mem lacks the key or holds an\r\n  212:   empty value (:1403-1413). A namespaced meta key written once SURVIVES every\r\n  213:   later save by construction.\r\n  214: - ROWS: row-level ownership. `_MERGE_OWNED_ROW_FIELDS` is a 19-field frozenset\r\n  215:   (text, char_count, word_count, traits, boundary, char_id, speaker_role,\r\n  216:   arc_phase, compose_flags, beat_intent, target_words, dialogue_slot_id, shot_id,\r\n  217:   beat_id, skip, tts_skip_reason, reviewer_skip_reason, reviewer_note,\r\n  218:   needs_render_realign + the music-cue spec fields) -- never resurrected from\r\n  219:   disk (:1441-1459). The merge boundary controls DISK COPY-FORWARD only; it is\r\n  220:   NOT a runtime mutation validator, and it is NOT the same field set as the\r\n  221:   direction DTO.\r\n  222: - The freeze audit hard-requires the fixed top-level list set and per-line shape\r\n  223:   (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:118-129, 252-404); it does not govern namespaced\r\n  224:   meta keys.\r\n  225: - Source-bank law: \"Evidence maps and authorship receipts live in typed artifacts\r\n  226:   or namespaced `meta`; the fixed line schema contains no ad hoc provenance\r\n  227:   fields\" (docs/SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md:184-186).\r\n  228: \r\n  229: ---\r\n  230: \r\n  231: ## 2. The typed artifact: `meta.visual_direction` (schema `vd-1`)\r\n  232: \r\n  233: ### 2.1 TWO models, not one (Lesson 2)\r\n  234: \r\n  235: A model cannot author its own `prompt_sha256`. The design has two typed models:\r\n  236: \r\n  237: - **`VisualDirectionDraftV1`** / **`VisualDirectionShotsBatchV1`** -- EXACTLY\r\n  238:   what the LLM returns. Pydantic `BaseModel`, `extra=\"forbid\"`, closed nested\r\n  239:   rows. These are the `schema=` passed to `structured_call`.\r\n  240: - **`VisualDirectionArtifactV1`** -- what Python ASSEMBLES and stamps: the drafts\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r4\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$n=240;$n -lt 480;$n++){ '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f (\"'$n+1),$lines[$n] }'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r4\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$n=240;$n -lt 480;$n++){ '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f (\"'$n+1),$lines[$n] }'","aggregated_output":"  241:   + the vetted safety base + the derived receipts + the seals. Never generated,\r\n  242:   never repaired, never LLM-touched.\r\n  243: \r\n  244: `nodes/_otr_visual_direction.py` is therefore NOT \"pure stdlib\" -- it imports\r\n  245: pydantic, lazily, like every other structured pass.\r\n  246: \r\n  247: **No `max_length` on any authored string (r3 codex M2 -- Lesson 3).**\r\n  248: `validate_tolerant_data` catches a `ValidationError`, CLAMPS over-long top-level\r\n  249: strings to their declared `max_length`, re-validates, and PROCEEDS with only a\r\n  250: `log.warning` (nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:422-434). On an authored visual\r\n  251: string that is a SILENT COERCION OF AUTHORED CONTENT -- precisely what Lesson 3\r\n  252: forbids. Because the clamp arm fires only on a `ValidationError`, declaring NO\r\n  253: `max_length` on authored strings disarms it completely. Every length bound is\r\n  254: enforced in the `post_validator` instead, which raises `PostValidationError` and\r\n  255: routes the failure to the TYPED REPAIR rung (4.5). No change to the shared\r\n  256: machinery; authored text either comes back correct or fails closed.\r\n  257: \r\n  258: ### 2.2 `VisualDirectionDraftV1` -- pass P-A's surface (closed set)\r\n  259: \r\n  260: ```json\r\n  261: {\r\n  262:   \"style_language\": \"<one-paragraph episode visual thesis>\",\r\n  263:   \"era_cues\": [\"<cue>\", \"...\"],\r\n  264:   \"motifs\": [ { \"motif\": \"<recurring visual motif>\",\r\n  265:                 \"evidence\": [ {\"id\": \"line:l0007\", \"quote\": \"<verbatim <=120 chars>\"} ] } ],\r\n  266:   \"clue_visual\": { \"treatment\": \"<how the clue mechanism reads on screen>\",\r\n  267:                    \"evidence\": [ {\"id\": \"line:l0012\", \"quote\": \"...\"} ] },\r\n  268: \r\n  269:   \"look\": {\r\n  270:     \"label\": \"...\", \"era_tail\": \"...\", \"positive_tail\": \"...\",\r\n  271:     \"image_grade_tail\": \"...\", \"broadcast_tail\": \"...\",\r\n  272:     \"portrait_look\": \"...\", \"portrait_instruction_look\": \"...\",\r\n  273:     \"scene_instruction_look\": \"...\", \"radio_object_look\": \"...\",\r\n  274:     \"plate_look\": \"...\", \"still_word_title_mood_style\": \"...\"\r\n  275:   },\r\n  276: \r\n  277:   \"field_evidence\": {\r\n  278:     \"look.era_tail\":      { \"evidence\": [ {\"id\": \"line:l0003\", \"quote\": \"...\"} ],\r\n  279:                             \"kind\": \"factual\" },\r\n  280:     \"look.portrait_look\": { \"evidence\": [ {\"id\": \"cast:c01\", \"quote\": \"...\"} ],\r\n  281:                             \"kind\": \"factual\" },\r\n  282:     \"style_language\":     { \"evidence\": [ {\"id\": \"title\"} ], \"kind\": \"rationale\" },\r\n  283:     \"era_cues\":           { \"evidence\": [ {\"id\": \"brief:atmosphere_line\"} ],\r\n  284:                             \"kind\": \"rationale\" }\r\n  285:   }\r\n  286: }\r\n  287: ```\r\n  288: \r\n  289: - `look` is the CLOSED authored whitelist -- exactly those 11 keys, no more, no\r\n  290:   fewer. `still_word_typography` / `still_word_backdrop` are NOT authored (2.4).\r\n  291: - **`field_evidence` keys are a CLOSED ENUM** of literal key names: the 11\r\n  292:   `look.*` keys + `style_language` + `era_cues`. They are NOT free-form JSON\r\n  293:   pointers or schema paths (r3 codex M12 -- rev 3 forbade schema-path keys in the\r\n  294:   prompt while requiring them in the schema).\r\n  295: - **Row-shaped items carry their evidence INLINE only** (`motifs[]`,\r\n  296:   `clue_visual`) -- never duplicated into `field_evidence`.\r\n  297: - An `evidence` item is `{id, quote?}`. A `factual` entry MUST carry a `quote`\r\n  298:   (<= 120 chars) that is a VERBATIM SUBSTRING of the cited item's text in the\r\n  299:   source DTO -- machine-checked in the `post_validator`. ID existence alone does\r\n  300:   not prove support (r1 codex M5; r3 codex M12, light form). A `rationale` entry\r\n  301:   needs only the `id`.\r\n  302: - `shots[]` is NOT in this model -- it is pass P-B (2.3, 4.4), whose draft is\r\n  303:   `VisualDirectionShotsBatchV1`:\r\n  304:   `{ \"shots\": [ { \"line_id\": \"...\", \"subject_note\": \"...\", \"mood\": \"<one register word>\",\r\n  305:   \"evidence\": [ {\"id\": \"line:<the same line_id>\", \"quote\": \"...\"} ] } ] }`.\r\n  306:   Every row must cite its OWN line.\r\n  307: \r\n  308: ### 2.3 `VisualDirectionArtifactV1` -- what Python stamps\r\n  309: \r\n  310: ```json\r\n  311: {\r\n  312:   \"schema_version\": \"vd-1\",\r\n  313:   \"created_utc\": \"2026-07-12T00:00:00+00:00\",\r\n  314:   \"writer\": { \"node\": \"OTR_DynamicStoryDirection\", \"node_rev\": \"<git short>\" },\r\n  315: \r\n  316:   \"model_receipt\": {\r\n  317:     \"slot\": \"creative\",\r\n  318:     \"requested_model\": \"<the handle requested>\",\r\n  319:     \"resolved_model\": \"<provider-reported concrete model, or null>\",\r\n  320:     \"provider\": \"<transformers | gguf | openrouter | comfy_credits | google_api>\",\r\n  321:     \"runtime_policy\": { \"...\": \"policy_from_meta snapshot\" },\r\n  322:     \"effective_sampling\": { \"...\": \"PROVIDER-EFFECTIVE values, or null where the\r\n  323:                             provider does not report them (4.3)\" },\r\n  324:     \"prompt_version\": \"vd-look-1 / vd-shots-1\",\r\n  325:     \"token_budget\": { \"context_cap\": 8192, \"pa_input\": 0, \"pa_reserved\": 0,\r\n  326:                       \"pb_batches\": [], \"repair_envelope\": 0 },\r\n  327:     \"attempt_journal\": [ { \"pass\": \"look\", \"batch\": null, \"rung\": \"base\",\r\n  328:                            \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"reason\": null,\r\n  329:                            \"prompt_sha256\": \"...\", \"accepted_sha256\": \"...\" } ],\r\n  330:     \"source_recheck\": \"clean\"\r\n  331:   },\r\n  332: \r\n  333:   \"story_binding\": {\r\n  334:     \"episode_id\": \"<ledger episode_id>\",\r\n  335:     \"freeze_verdict\": \"frozen_clean\",\r\n  336:     \"freeze_timestamp\": \"<meta.freeze_timestamp verbatim>\",\r\n  337:     \"source_sha256\": \"<canonical sha256 of DirectionSourceV1, 2.5>\"\r\n  338:   },\r\n  339: \r\n  340:   \"rationale\": { \"style_language\": \"...\", \"era_cues\": [ ... ],\r\n  341:                  \"motifs\": [ ... ], \"clue_visual\": { ... } },\r\n  342: \r\n  343:   \"style_pack\": {\r\n  344:     \"style_id\": \"dynamic_story\", \"schema_version\": \"v2\", \"is_dynamic\": true,\r\n  345:     \"...\": \"the COMPLETE v2 field set -- ASSEMBLED from the vetted safety base\r\n  346:             + the draft's `look` -- validated by the SAME _validate_row rules\r\n  347:             (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:184+)\"\r\n  348:   },\r\n  349:   \"authored_fields\": [\"era_tail\", \"positive_tail\", \"...\"],\r\n  350:   \"field_evidence\": { \"<the draft map, verbatim>\": {} },\r\n  351: \r\n  352:   \"shots\": [ { \"line_id\": \"...\", \"subject_note\": \"...\", \"mood\": \"...\",\r\n  353:                \"evidence\": [ ... ] } ],\r\n  354: \r\n  355:   \"semantic_sha256\": \"<see below>\",\r\n  356:   \"artifact_sha256\": \"<canonical sha256 of the whole object minus this field>\"\r\n  357: }\r\n  358: ```\r\n  359: \r\n  360: **Hash discipline (enumerated key-for-key).** `binding` below is a DERIVED\r\n  361: two-key object built from `story_binding` -- it is NOT the `story_binding` object\r\n  362: (r3 antigravity M1). `freeze_timestamp` and `freeze_verdict` are volatile across\r\n  363: a re-freeze of the same content, so they are EXCLUDED from the semantic seal and\r\n  364: INCLUDED in the envelope seal:\r\n  365: \r\n  366: ```\r\n  367: semantic_sha256 = canonical_sha256({\r\n  368:     \"schema_version\":  <str>,\r\n  369:     \"style_pack\":      <the assembled v2 pack>,\r\n  370:     \"authored_fields\": <sorted list>,\r\n  371:     \"field_evidence\":  <map>,\r\n  372:     \"shots\":           <list, source-line order>,\r\n  373:     \"rationale\":       <object>,\r\n  374:     \"binding\": { \"episode_id\": <str>, \"source_sha256\": <str> }\r\n  375: })\r\n  376: artifact_sha256 = canonical_sha256(<whole artifact minus artifact_sha256>)\r\n  377: ```\r\n  378: \r\n  379: Both are RECOMPUTED on every read (7.1). `created_utc` and `model_receipt` sit\r\n  380: outside the semantic hash.\r\n  381: \r\n  382: The canonicalizer must be STRICT JSON-only: it REJECTS non-JSON values, NaN,\r\n  383: infinity, and non-string object keys. The existing helper\r\n  384: (nodes/production_ledger.py:292-302) falls back to `repr()` and never raises --\r\n  385: correct for a log line, wrong for a fail-closed seal.\r\n  386: \r\n  387: `content_mutations` is CUT as a stored field (it would always be the constant 0).\r\n  388: The CHECK stays (5.2 step 6, refuse the stamp on any delta); its outcome is\r\n  389: recorded once as `model_receipt.source_recheck`.\r\n  390: \r\n  391: ### 2.4 Who authors which pack field (the safety split)\r\n  392: \r\n  393: - **Vetted safety base (checked-in Python constant, operator-owned; not\r\n  394:   LLM-touched):** `portrait_look_talking` (S4b lip-sync law -- bright/frontal/\r\n  395:   warm, nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:160-168), `announcer_subject_face`,\r\n  396:   `announcer_subject_ltx_mouth` (mouth-vocabulary contract,\r\n  397:   nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:117-119), `announcer_subject_object`,\r\n  398:   `open_subjects` ({form} templates), `motion_registers` (240-char engine budget,\r\n  399:   :121-123), `non_character_emblem_fallback`, `allow_radio_tails`,\r\n  400:   `forbidden_terms`, **and `still_word_typography` + `still_word_backdrop` in\r\n  401:   their entirety (D5 CLOSED)** -- every nested dict the LLM authors is another\r\n  402:   wrong-depth failure surface (4.5) and another 200-400 output tokens against an\r\n  403:   8192 cap. Reopen post-v1.\r\n  404: - **LLM-authored look whitelist:** exactly the 11 keys of\r\n  405:   `VisualDirectionDraftV1.look`.\r\n  406: - `authored_fields` is DERIVED (Python writes it from the whitelist) and is the\r\n  407:   machine-checkable proof the assembly obeyed the split.\r\n  408: - The anti-geometry lint over authored fields uses a PYTHON-OWNED fixed\r\n  409:   vocabulary (framing/headroom/crop/close-up/mouth-visibility terms), never the\r\n  410:   artifact's own `forbidden_terms` (an LLM must not author its own guard).\r\n  411: \r\n  412: ### 2.5 `DirectionSourceV1` -- the ONE source DTO, and its per-pass VIEWS\r\n  413: \r\n  414: ONE closed DTO is simultaneously (a) the hash preimage and (b) the evidence\r\n  415: universe. Nothing may be cited that is not in it.\r\n  416: \r\n  417: | Collection | EXACT fields (closed set) | null normalization |\r\n  418: |---|---|---|\r\n  419: | `meta` | episode_title, style, source_bank, visual_style | str: `\"\"` |\r\n  420: | `brief` | atmosphere_line, visual_palette, key_objects, lighting, story_brief_terms | str: `\"\"`; list: `[]` |\r\n  421: | `cast[]` | char_id, name, gender, traits, character_description | str: `\"\"`; list: `[]` |\r\n  422: | `lines[]` | line_id, text, char_id, speaker_role, boundary, skip, tts_skip_reason | str: `\"\"`; **bool `skip`: `false`** |\r\n  423: \r\n  424: Rows in ledger order; keys sorted; per-type normalization (a blanket `null -> \"\"`\r\n  425: would corrupt the boolean `skip` and the list-valued brief fields -- r3 codex M4).\r\n  426: `story_brief_terms` lives under `brief` ONLY (rev 3 duplicated it under `meta`).\r\n  427: Any field NOT listed is omitted -- audio timing, voice presets, word counts,\r\n  428: reviewer notes are all post-freeze or non-authored, and excluding them BY DESIGN\r\n  429: is what makes the hash stable across ShotLock's in-place timing overlay\r\n  430: (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:169-221) and CastLock's post-freeze voice assignment\r\n  431: (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:493-502).\r\n  432: \r\n  433: `source_sha256 = canonical_sha256(DirectionSourceV1)`. Writer and readers compute\r\n  434: it with ONE shared pure helper so the two sides can never drift.\r\n  435: **No `beats` row** -- there is no such array (1.3).\r\n  436: \r\n  437: **Per-pass VIEWS (each a NAMED, DEFINED projection of the DTO):**\r\n  438: \r\n  439: - `DirectionSourceView_PA`: `meta` + `brief` + full `cast[]` + a LINE SPINE\r\n  440:   (`line_id`, `char_id`, `speaker_role`, `boundary`, `skip`, and `text` in full\r\n  441:   if the exact-preflight fits it, else a deterministic head truncation to the\r\n  442:   measured budget -- the truncation POINT is recorded in the receipt).\r\n  443: - `DirectionSourceView_PB(batch)`: the authored `look` from P-A + FULL `text` for\r\n  444:   the lines in this batch + the cast rows those lines reference.\r\n  445: \r\n  446: **Cite-only-what-you-saw:** an evidence `id` must resolve in the DTO AND be\r\n  447: present in the VIEW the citing pass received. A pass cannot cite a line it never\r\n  448: read.\r\n  449: \r\n  450: ### 2.6 Evidence grammar, and the `shots[]` universe\r\n  451: \r\n  452: IDs: `line:<line_id>`, `cast:<char_id>`, `meta:<key>`, `brief:<key>`, `title`.\r\n  453: `beat:` is RETIRED -- there is no ledger beat at direction time (1.3).\r\n  454: \r\n  455: **The `shots[]` universe is the STILL-TARGET SET, not \"every line\" (r3\r\n  456: antigravity M4).** A row exists ONLY for a line that actually yields a scene\r\n  457: still or a word card, and that set is computed by the SAME pure target-derivation\r\n  458: helper MetaBrief uses (`derive_scene_still_targets` / `_iter_beat_lines`,\r\n  459: nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1016+). Exactly one row per target, in\r\n  460: source-line order, no omissions, unique `line_id`. `b000_music_open` is OUT OF\r\n  461: SCOPE (it does not exist at direction time; the opening-music scene keeps its\r\n  462: pack-level treatment). Consumption is MANDATORY and per-kind (7.4) -- an authored\r\n  463: note that nothing consumes is dead scope.\r\n  464: \r\n  465: ### 2.7 Deliberately OUT of vd-1 (cuts, judged)\r\n  466: \r\n  467: - `scenes[]` (no canonical scene key); `global.continuity` (`meta.continuity`\r\n  468:   already has one owner, nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:4721-4746; character look\r\n  469:   is carried by the cast rows, nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:116-153); wardrobe\r\n  470:   (`OTR_OUTFIT_LOCK` stays the authority, :143-153); executable\r\n  471:   `composition_rules` (geometry law) -- all CUT in r1.\r\n  472: - `rationale.composition_notes` -- non-executable BY CONSTRUCTION, so pure schema\r\n  473:   + context budget. CUT (r2).\r\n  474: - `story_binding.content_mutations` -- an always-zero stored constant. CUT (r3);\r\n  475:   the check survives as `model_receipt.source_recheck`.\r\n  476: - still_word typography/backdrop authorship -- CUT from v1 (2.4).\r\n  477: - Reroll/revision machinery, and with it ARTIFACT HISTORY -- CUT from v1 (7.5).\r\n  478:   The provenance digest is scoped to the CURRENT artifact; \"which historical\r\n  479:   artifact authored this cached pixel\" is explicitly not a v1 promise.\r\n  480: - Credits/dossier integration -- CUT.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r4\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$n=480;$n -lt 720;$n++){ '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f (\"'$n+1),$lines[$n] }'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r4\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$n=480;$n -lt 720;$n++){ '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f (\"'$n+1),$lines[$n] }'","aggregated_output":"  481: \r\n  482: `rationale.motifs` / `clue_visual` / `era_cues` are KEPT but NON-EXECUTABLE:\r\n  483: nothing composes prompts from them; they are the evidence-bound reasoning behind\r\n  484: the pack tails, and the audit walk reads them (7.6).\r\n  485: \r\n  486: ---\r\n  487: \r\n  488: ## 3. Ownership (Lesson 1)\r\n  489: \r\n  490: ### 3.1 Actors\r\n  491: \r\n  492: | Actor | Role | Grounding |\r\n  493: |---|---|---|\r\n  494: | OTR_DynamicStoryDirection (NEW node) | SOLE writer of `meta.visual_direction`. Post-freeze, reads the frozen ledger read-only, stamps the artifact, forwards patched `script_json`. Pure pass-through when the sentinel is not selected. | Insertion at the 62.out[1] VISUAL fan-out (links 255/252, 1.4) |\r\n  495: | OTR_LedgerScriptWriter | Writes `meta.visual_style` only (now possibly the sentinel). Never writes `visual_direction`. | :3651-3655 |\r\n  496: | `resolve_visual_direction(ledger) -> ResolvedDirection` (NEW seam) | The ONE reader. Validates the artifact against the ledger and returns a typed BUNDLE: `{style: VisualStyle, shots_by_line_id: dict, semantic_sha256: str, artifact_meta: dict}` -- a bare `VisualStyle` cannot carry the mandatory shots index or the digest (r3 codex M7). `_resolve_style`/`get_visual_style` stay meta-only for named packs. | 5.3 |\r\n  497: | OTR_MetaBriefImagePromptGen | Consumer + MANDATORY consumer of `shots[]` per the 7.4 matrix. **Signature change required** -- `derive_image_prompts` today takes no ledger and resolves meta-only. Also gains a `finally` LLM teardown. | :1570-1574, 1601-1609, 2087-2096, 2137-2168 |\r\n  498: | OTR_ShotLock | Consumer; resolves BEFORE the beat loop, outside the fail-soft block. Also gains a `finally` LLM teardown. | :626-636, 651-697 |\r\n  499: | render_driver | THIRD independent resolver -- must resolve through the new seam and honor the dynamic look authority in its brief-core branch. | :1248, 2069, 2080 |\r\n  500: | OTR_ImageGenDispatcher | Persists the direction digest + composed prompt on image rows, on BOTH the cache-miss and cache-HIT paths (a hit CLONES the old row, :627-632). | :117-129, 603-643, 796-826 |\r\n  501: \r\n  502: ### 3.2 Field-level ownership (authored | derived | measured)\r\n  503: \r\n  504: | Field | Class | Writer |\r\n  505: |---|---|---|\r\n  506: | `style_pack.<11 look keys>` | AUTHORED | direction LLM (P-A) |\r\n  507: | `style_pack.<all other v2 keys>` | AUTHORED (offline) | operator, in the checked-in safety base |\r\n  508: | `rationale.*` | AUTHORED | direction LLM (P-A), non-executable |\r\n  509: | `field_evidence` | AUTHORED | direction LLM (P-A) |\r\n  510: | `shots[]` | AUTHORED | direction LLM (P-B, batched) |\r\n  511: | `authored_fields` | DERIVED | Python (from the whitelist) |\r\n  512: | `story_binding.source_sha256` | DERIVED | Python |\r\n  513: | `story_binding.episode_id / freeze_verdict / freeze_timestamp` | DERIVED | Python (verbatim from meta) |\r\n  514: | `model_receipt.*` (provider, effective sampling, token_budget, attempt_journal, source_recheck) | MEASURED | Python (from the cache entry, the preflight, and the ladder) |\r\n  515: | `semantic_sha256` / `artifact_sha256` | DERIVED | Python |\r\n  516: | `created_utc` | MEASURED | Python |\r\n  517: \r\n  518: ### 3.3 Closed nested-row field sets\r\n  519: \r\n  520: - `shots[]` row: EXACTLY `{line_id, subject_note, mood, evidence}`.\r\n  521: - `field_evidence` entry: EXACTLY `{evidence: [EvidenceItem], kind:\r\n  522:   \"factual\"|\"rationale\"}`; its KEY is from the closed enum (2.2).\r\n  523: - `EvidenceItem`: EXACTLY `{id, quote?}`; `quote` REQUIRED when `kind ==\r\n  524:   \"factual\"`.\r\n  525: - `rationale.motifs[]` row: EXACTLY `{motif, evidence}`.\r\n  526: - `clue_visual`: EXACTLY `{treatment, evidence}`.\r\n  527: - Any extra key at any depth = schema failure (`extra=\"forbid\"`).\r\n  528: \r\n  529: ---\r\n  530: \r\n  531: ## 4. The LLM derivation contract (Lessons 2, 3, 4, 5)\r\n  532: \r\n  533: ### 4.1 Five representations, in lockstep\r\n  534: \r\n  535: | # | Representation | Where it lives |\r\n  536: |---|---|---|\r\n  537: | 1 | base prompt | NEW `nodes/_otr_visual_direction_prompts.py` -- a FEATURE prompt module, matching the two existing `*_prompts.py` modules. **NOT a story-pack seam:** pack seams are PER-SOURCE-BANK (`PRODUCTION_SEAM_ALLOWLIST`, nodes/_otr_story_pack.py:27-44; unknown seam = `UnknownSeamError`, :146-151), and visual direction is orthogonal to the bank -- all 11 packs would otherwise have to author it. |\r\n  538: | 2 | typed schema | `VisualDirectionDraftV1` + `VisualDirectionShotsBatchV1` (pydantic, `extra=\"forbid\"`, NO `max_length` on authored strings -- 2.1). |\r\n  539: | 3 | worked fixture | **TWO fixtures, one per pass**, under `tests/fixtures/`, each EMBEDDED verbatim in its own base prompt. |\r\n  540: | 4 | parser + validator | `parse_first_json_object` (nodes/_otr_json.py:81) / `parse_validate_tolerant` (nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:442) + a per-pass `post_validator`. **Never hand-roll brace slicing** -- `_parse_directives` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:429-451) is the anti-pattern: it slices `find(\"{\")`/`rfind(\"}\")` and returns `{}` SILENTLY. |\r\n  541: | 5 | repair prompt | Per failure class, PER PASS (4.5). |\r\n  542: \r\n  543: Message assembly follows the proven pattern\r\n  544: (nodes/_otr_scifi_codex.py:1156-1160): seam text + `schema_shape_instruction`\r\n  545: (nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:195) as SYSTEM; a deterministic sorted-key JSON\r\n  546: envelope (the pass VIEW + the JSON schema + the worked fixture) as USER.\r\n  547: \r\n  548: **The prompt must explicitly FORBID the known pseudo-shapes** (Lesson 2):\r\n  549: numbered fields (`era_tail_2`), `_secondary`/`_tertiary` variants, invented\r\n  550: schema-path keys, singular-vs-list aliases (`shot` vs `shots`), and **valid\r\n  551: collections nested at the WRONG DEPTH**. That last class is the highest-\r\n  552: probability live failure of this feature and it is already logged TWICE, this\r\n  553: week, on the second local family: PBUG-20260712-02 (nested `causal_steps` inside\r\n  554: `caller_threads` rows) and PBUG-20260712-03 (nested `shots` inside `scenes` rows)\r\n  555: -- docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md. Each pass's prompt states ITS OWN collections' exact\r\n  556: top-level ownership (P-A owns `motifs` / `field_evidence`; P-B owns `shots`), and\r\n  557: the repair ladder carries the deterministic relocation rung (4.5).\r\n  558: \r\n  559: ### 4.2 Slot and model (D2 CLOSED -- `creative`)\r\n  560: \r\n  561: The slot comment (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:405-411) reads \"technical =\r\n  562: structured passes\", which naively argues `technical` for any JSON pass. But the\r\n  563: operative rule is PASS NATURE, and fable2 proves it: P0 dossier (extraction) runs\r\n  564: on **technical** (nodes/_otr_scifi_fable2.py:1129-1137), while P1 pitch room, P2b\r\n  565: treatment and P3 whole-play markup -- all authorship, all schema-constrained JSON\r\n  566: through `structured_call` -- run on **creative** (:1166-1174, :1201-1209, :1394).\r\n  567: Visual direction is authorship. **`creative`.**\r\n  568: \r\n  569: - Model id: `meta[\"creative_writing_model\"]` (stamped\r\n  570:   nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:1421-1422; the read-from-meta idiom is\r\n  571:   nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:663-665), resolved fail-loud through\r\n  572:   `require_model(model_id, slot=\"creative\")` (nodes/_otr_model_inputs.py:72).\r\n  573: - Entry: `request_slot(\"creative\", model_id, policy=policy_from_meta(meta))`\r\n  574:   (nodes/_otr_model_loader.py:790, 821-824; nodes/_otr_shared/llm_policy.py:131).\r\n  575: - **Two signatures, do not mix them.** `structured_call` needs\r\n  576:   `slot_fn(messages, *, temperature, max_new_tokens) -> str` (the\r\n  577:   `make_generate_fn` shape). ShotLock's `llm_fn` is the DIFFERENT\r\n  578:   `callable(prompt: str) -> str` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:513-516). The test\r\n  579:   injection for this node uses the GenerateFn shape.\r\n  580: \r\n  581: ### 4.3 The provider-effective interface (r3 codex M6 -- Lesson 5)\r\n  582: \r\n  583: `_otr_model_loader.make_generate_fn`'s local lane (:1108-1137) applies the chat\r\n  584: template, tokenizes, and calls `model.generate` -- with **no `max_input_tokens`\r\n  585: computation, no truncation warning, and no must-fit honoring**. `context_cap` sits\r\n  586: on the cache entry and is IGNORED there. The guard exists ONLY inside the writer's\r\n  587: own slot wrapper (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:664-699): `max_input_tokens =\r\n  588: max(64, context_cap - int(max_new_tokens))` (:681), then either\r\n  589: `raise PromptContextOverflowError(\"... refusing to left-truncate an unsliceable\r\n  590: provenance prompt\")` when the messages object carries the must-fit marker\r\n  591: (:684-690; marker `_PromptMustFitMessages`, nodes/_otr_scifi_codex.py:308-311) or\r\n  592: a LEFT-truncating `PROMPT_GUARD` (:691-699). PROMPT_GUARD truncation of a typed\r\n  593: repair is the root-cause chain in PBUG-20260712-03.\r\n  594: \r\n  595: And the guard cannot simply be copied, because **remote lanes have no HF\r\n  596: tokenizer to measure with**, OpenRouter/Comfy floor the output reservation, and\r\n  597: providers may override temperature/caps\r\n  598: (nodes/_otr_openrouter_backend.py:905-985; nodes/_otr_comfy_backend.py:426-480;\r\n  599: nodes/_otr_google_api/llm.py:115-162; nodes/_otr_gguf_backend.py:393-402).\r\n  600: \r\n  601: **REQUIREMENT: ONE provider-effective interface**, used identically by the\r\n  602: preflight, the invocation, and the receipt, exposing per cache entry:\r\n  603: `context_cap`, `count_tokens(messages) -> int` (HF tokenizer locally; the\r\n  604: provider's own accounting or a conservative estimator remotely),\r\n  605: `effective_max_new_tokens(requested) -> int` (honoring provider floors), and\r\n  606: `effective_sampling() -> dict | null`. The direction pass RAISES on overflow and\r\n  607: NEVER truncates. Unknown values land in the receipt as `null`, not as invented\r\n  608: numbers.\r\n  609: \r\n  610: **Constrained generation** is a LANE feature, not a slot feature:\r\n  611: `make_constrained_generate_fn` (nodes/_otr_constrained_generate.py:161) binds\r\n  612: lm-format-enforcer on the local HF lane (:262-269) and maps the same pydantic\r\n  613: schema to `response_format` on openrouter / comfy_credits / gguf_native\r\n  614: (:207-238). **Google has NO branch** -- so the cloud qualification leg (9.2)\r\n  615: either adds one or explicitly runs unconstrained with the repair ladder as its\r\n  616: only defense. State which.\r\n  617: \r\n  618: ### 4.4 Budgets, and why it is TWO passes (D8 CLOSED)\r\n  619: \r\n  620: `DEFAULT_LLM = \"mistralai/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407\"`\r\n  621: (nodes/_otr_model_catalog.py:32) backs both slots by default; `resolve_context_cap`\r\n  622: (:1258) clamps to `HARD_VRAM_CONTEXT_LIMIT`, default **8192** (:1207-1217), and\r\n  623: Mistral-Nemo is CURATED to 8192 (:1226-1234).\r\n  624: \r\n  625: One vd-1 object cannot fit: 11 look strings + rationale + evidence + one `shots[]`\r\n  626: row per still target (a 420-word episode carries roughly 40-60 lines) -- and the\r\n  627: input carries every line's text + the brief + the schema + the fixture. Sizing\r\n  628: from `target_words` is exactly what Lesson 5 forbids.\r\n  629: \r\n  630: **Two pass classes, one artifact, one hash:**\r\n  631: \r\n  632: - **P-A (look).** ONE call. Input: `DirectionSourceView_PA`. Output:\r\n  633:   `VisualDirectionDraftV1`.\r\n  634: - **P-B (shots).** BATCHED over still targets, mirroring the existing batching\r\n  635:   seam `derive_creative_directives(..., batch_size: int = 15, ...)`\r\n  636:   (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:499-508). Input: `DirectionSourceView_PB(batch)`.\r\n  637:   Output: `VisualDirectionShotsBatchV1`.\r\n  638: \r\n  639: **Preflight, in the only order that can execute (r3 codex M5 + antigravity M2):**\r\n  640: \r\n  641: 1. `request_slot` FIRST (inside the teardown-protected region, 5.2) -- there is\r\n  642:    no `context_cap` and no tokenizer before a cache entry exists.\r\n  643: 2. EXACT preflight of P-A: `count_tokens(P-A messages) +\r\n  644:    effective_max_new_tokens(pa_reserve) + REPAIR_ENVELOPE <= context_cap`.\r\n  645: 3. SCHEMA-MAXIMUM preflight of P-B BEFORE any generation: the worst legal batch\r\n  646:    (batch_size rows, each at the maximum legal `subject_note` length + evidence +\r\n  647:    JSON overhead), so an impossible budget fails before the first token is spent.\r\n  648: 4. Run P-A. Then EXACT-preflight each real P-B batch before it is sent.\r\n  649: \r\n  650: `REPAIR_ENVELOPE` is COMPUTED, not guessed: the typed-repair call re-sends the\r\n  651: original prompt + the failed output echo + the directive and must itself generate\r\n  652: a full response, so the worst-case rung needs roughly\r\n  653: `input + 2 * max_new_tokens + len(directive)`. Measure the directive; do not\r\n  654: hard-code a magic number.\r\n  655: \r\n  656: `batch_size` and the output reservations are DERIVED FROM THE MEASURED MAXIMA of\r\n  657: that arithmetic. (The starting figures 15 / ~900 tokens are a PLACEHOLDER for\r\n  658: Codex's measurement, not a specification: 15 legal 240-char notes plus evidence\r\n  659: and JSON overhead already exceed 900 tokens.)\r\n  660: \r\n  661: Bounds (enforced in `post_validator`, never as `max_length` -- 2.1):\r\n  662: `subject_note <= 240` chars (mirrors the motion budget,\r\n  663: nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:121-123); `quote <= 120` chars; every authored string\r\n  664: bounded; assembled artifact `<= 64 KB` canonical (a STORAGE bound, not a context\r\n  665: budget).\r\n  666: \r\n  667: ### 4.5 The repair ladder (Lessons 3, 4) -- reuse `structured_call`\r\n  668: \r\n  669: `structured_call(*, prompt, schema, slot_fn, base_temperature,\r\n  670: structural_retry_temperature, repair_prompt_factory, post_validator,\r\n  671: max_new_tokens, max_attempts, helper_name)` (nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:551).\r\n  672: Its rungs ARE Lesson 4:\r\n  673: \r\n  674: 1. base attempt at `base_temperature` (:668-689);\r\n  675: 2. structural retry -- SAME prompt, LOWER temperature, ONLY on\r\n  676:    `json.JSONDecodeError` (:700-721); a schema/content failure deliberately SKIPS\r\n  677:    this rung (:691-699);\r\n  678: 3. typed repair at `_REPAIR_TEMPERATURE = 0.10` (:83, :724-775); the factory\r\n  679:    receives the original prompt, the failed raw output, and the exception\r\n  680:    (nodes/_otr_repair_prompts.py:128-152);\r\n  681: 4. repair-syntax retry -- re-sends the EXACT cached repair prompt once (:783-811,\r\n  682:    floor `_REPAIR_SYNTAX_RETRY_FLOOR = 0.25` at :89).\r\n  683: \r\n  684: `max_attempts = 3` (`_DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS`, :69). Entry invariant, fails loud:\r\n  685: `structural_retry_temperature` MUST be strictly lower than `base_temperature`\r\n  686: (:640-648). Exhaustion raises `StructuredCallFailedError` (:97, :819-823) -- never\r\n  687: a sentinel. Existing factories + dispatcher: nodes/_otr_repair_prompts.py:164,\r\n  688: :184, :204, :231, :250, :271, :290, :321, `make_dispatching_repair_factory`:402.\r\n  689: \r\n  690: `post_validator` (typed `PostValidationError`, :128, raised :435-438) carries\r\n  691: EVERY deterministic CONTENT check: evidence-ID resolution against the DTO **and\r\n  692: against the pass's own VIEW**, the quote-substring check, the Python geometry\r\n  693: lint, the authored-vs-safety-base collision check, all length bounds, `line_id`\r\n  694: membership/uniqueness against the still-target set, and P-B aggregate set equality\r\n  695: (every target covered, none invented).\r\n  696: \r\n  697: | Failure class | Rung | Deterministic repair (no LLM call, :750-761) |\r\n  698: |---|---|---|\r\n  699: | undecodable JSON | structural retry (same prompt, lower temp) | no |\r\n  700: | wrong-depth collection, WITHIN THIS PASS's own collections (P-A: `motifs`, `field_evidence`; P-B: `shots`) | typed repair naming the exact top-level ownership | **YES, and only here:** an authoritative top-level collection wins; a nested one is lifted VERBATIM only when top-level is absent/empty AND the destination is unique (or all candidates are byte-identical). The factory must then validate the COMPLETE contract -- schema AND post_validator -- before returning; a partially valid object must NOT consume the rung (Lesson 3; PBUG-20260712-02/-03 fix pattern). Cross-pass relocation is impossible and must not be attempted. |\r\n  701: | other schema/field shape | typed repair (`schema_field_repair` style) | no |\r\n  702: | unresolvable evidence ID, or an ID outside this pass's VIEW | typed repair naming the invariant + the owning key | no |\r\n  703: | missing or non-substring `quote` on a `factual` entry | typed repair naming the cited line's text | no |\r\n  704: | over-long authored string (note, quote, tail) | **typed repair** -- reached via `post_validator`, never a silent clamp (2.1) | no |\r\n  705: | geometry / forbidden term in an authored field | typed repair naming the term + the field | no |\r\n  706: | authored field outside the whitelist | typed repair naming the whitelist | **no** -- stripping it would accept an LLM write where it must not |\r\n  707: | P-B batch misses a target, invents a `line_id`, or duplicates one | typed repair naming the exact legal id set for THIS batch | no |\r\n  708: | ladder exhausted | `StructuredCallFailedError` -> named domain error -> episode ABORTS | fail closed |\r\n  709: \r\n  710: **Attempt journal.** `structured_call` today returns only the accepted model and\r\n  711: exposes no rung/outcome hook, so a caller-side wrapper can hash raw calls but\r\n  712: cannot know which rung fired or why (r3 codex M8). The design adds an OPTIONAL\r\n  713: attempt-event sink to `structured_call` (an additive, backward-compatible\r\n  714: parameter -- section 8) that emits `{pass, batch, rung, outcome, reason,\r\n  715: effective_config, prompt_sha256, accepted_sha256}` per attempt. Receipts store\r\n  716: ACCEPTED-state hashes and reasons -- never rejected raw model output.\r\n  717: \r\n  718: ---\r\n  719: \r\n  720: ## 5. Lifecycle and storage\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r4\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$n=720;$n -lt 960;$n++){ '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f (\"'$n+1),$lines[$n] }'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$lines=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r4\\\\input.md'; for(\"'$n=720;$n -lt 960;$n++){ '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f (\"'$n+1),$lines[$n] }'","aggregated_output":"  721: \r\n  722: ### 5.1 Location: `meta.visual_direction`. Nothing else is ledger-safe.\r\n  723: \r\n  724: Top-level is ruled out by the merge code (only `TOP_PRESERVE` survives,\r\n  725: nodes/production_ledger.py:1387-1393) and by the freeze audit's top-level pin\r\n  726: (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:118-129). Line/cast rows are ruled out by row\r\n  727: ownership (:1441-1459) and the preflight law\r\n  728: (docs/SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md:184-186). META survives by construction\r\n  729: (:1403-1413) -- exactly how `meta.visual_style`, `meta.freeze_*`,\r\n  730: `meta.gap_audit_*` persist today.\r\n  731: \r\n  732: ### 5.2 Write path (order is load-bearing -- r3 codex M9)\r\n  733: \r\n  734: 1. Preconditions (ALL fail-closed): `meta.visual_style == \"dynamic_story\"`;\r\n  735:    `meta.cleanup_locked is True`; `meta.freeze_verdict` in\r\n  736:    `{frozen_clean, frozen_with_warns}` (`needs_full_rerun` refuses,\r\n  737:    nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:787-811); **`meta.freeze_unload_ok is True`** (a\r\n  738:    still-resident writer LLM plus a fresh creative LLM is an OOM on 16 GB;\r\n  739:    nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:453-478); non-empty `lines`/`cast`.\r\n  740: 2. Build `DirectionSourceV1`; compute `source_sha256` (2.5). Derive the\r\n  741:    still-target set with MetaBrief's own helper (2.6).\r\n  742: 3. `request_slot` -- and from here to step 6 everything runs inside the\r\n  743:    teardown-protected region.\r\n  744: 4. Preflight P-A exactly + P-B at schema maximum (4.4). Overflow raises HERE.\r\n  745: 5. P-A, then the P-B batches, via `structured_call` (4.5).\r\n  746: 6. Assemble the pack (safety base + authored `look`); validate the whole artifact:\r\n  747:    embedded pack through `_validate_row` (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:184+),\r\n  748:    evidence + quote resolution, geometry lint, whitelist collision, shots coverage\r\n  749:    against the target set. REBUILD `DirectionSourceV1` from the live ledger and\r\n  750:    REFUSE to stamp on any delta (`model_receipt.source_recheck`).\r\n  751: 7. **`finally`: LLM teardown** (5.5). If teardown RAISES: persist the failed\r\n  752:    receipt and RE-RAISE -- do NOT proceed to GPU image work with a resident LLM.\r\n  753: 8. ONLY AFTER a successful teardown: seal (`semantic_sha256`, `artifact_sha256`),\r\n  754:    stamp `meta.visual_direction` on the wire ledger, persist via\r\n  755:    `stamp_durable(meta_updates={\"visual_direction\": ...})`\r\n  756:    (nodes/production_ledger.py:408-422), re-serialize `script_json`, emit `done`.\r\n  757:    Before the durable stamp: `peek = peek_ledger()` -- it can return `None`\r\n  758:    (:372-397) -- and raise if `peek is None` or its `episode_id` differs from the\r\n  759:    wire ledger's.\r\n  760: \r\n  761: ### 5.3 Read path: `resolve_visual_direction(ledger) -> ResolvedDirection`\r\n  762: \r\n  763: `get_visual_style(meta)` cannot enforce the staleness matrix -- it never sees the\r\n  764: arrays (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:378-390). ONE new ledger-aware function\r\n  765: validates the artifact and returns a TYPED BUNDLE:\r\n  766: `{style: VisualStyle, shots_by_line_id: dict[str, ShotNote], semantic_sha256: str,\r\n  767: artifact_meta: dict}`. A bare `VisualStyle` would force consumers to re-read\r\n  768: unvalidated `meta` for the notes and the digest.\r\n  769: \r\n  770: Three consumer entries; **two need a signature change**:\r\n  771: \r\n  772: - **MetaBrief:** `generate()` holds the parsed `led`\r\n  773:   (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:2137-2144) -- it resolves there and passes\r\n  774:   the bundle down. `derive_image_prompts` gains `style=None` and\r\n  775:   `shots_by_line_id=None` instead of calling `_resolve_style(meta)` itself\r\n  776:   (:1570-1574, :1609). The threaded style must reach EVERY prompt branch.\r\n  777: - **ShotLock:** holds the whole `led` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1040); resolves ONCE\r\n  778:   before the beat loop, outside the fail-soft block (7.2).\r\n  779: - **render_driver:** resolves once at the episode entry and threads the bundle\r\n  780:   through the shot-request builders instead of calling `get_visual_style(meta)` at\r\n  781:   :1248.\r\n  782: \r\n  783: REJECTED (r1): reading the `peek_ledger()` process singleton inside\r\n  784: `get_visual_style` -- consumers operate on the WIRE ledger, and the singleton can\r\n  785: lag or be absent.\r\n  786: \r\n  787: The dynamic `VisualStyle` NEVER enters the module pack cache (`_STYLES`,\r\n  788: nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:170, 355-359); it is built per resolve from the\r\n  789: artifact.\r\n  790: \r\n  791: ### 5.4 Look authority on the dynamic lane (BOTH lanes)\r\n  792: \r\n  793: The brief outranks the pack for the era tail today\r\n  794: (nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:356-370, 401, 414, 428), and the VIDEO lane has\r\n  795: a second brief-first core: `core = get_story_brief_ltx(_meta)`\r\n  796: (nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_driver.py:2069).\r\n  797: \r\n  798: **Rule: on the dynamic lane the artifact pack is the SOLE final-look authority in\r\n  799: BOTH lanes; the brief is evidence INPUT to the direction LLM, not a runtime\r\n  800: override.** `get_era_tail`, the palette reads in the still/portrait profiles, and\r\n  801: render_driver's brief-core branch must all use the pack-authored tail when the\r\n  802: resolved style `is_dynamic`. The derivation prompt receives the brief verbatim (it\r\n  803: is IN `DirectionSourceV1`), so brief specifics reach the final look THROUGH the\r\n  804: authored pack, with evidence recorded.\r\n  805: \r\n  806: D10 CLOSED: the dynamic lane is signalled by the `is_dynamic` BOOLEAN on the\r\n  807: resolved `VisualStyle`, not by a `style_id == \"dynamic_story\"` string compare\r\n  808: scattered through the helper family.\r\n  809: \r\n  810: ### 5.5 VRAM: a teardown BARRIER, not one node's `finally`\r\n  811: \r\n  812: The direction node's own unload does NOT keep VRAM at baseline before image\r\n  813: dispatch: MetaBrief immediately RE-RESOLVES the writer LLM\r\n  814: (`_resolve_writer_llm(meta, warnings)`, nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:\r\n  815: 2087-2096, called at :2158, delegating to ShotLock's resolver at\r\n  816: nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:651-697), and neither node unloads before returning.\r\n  817: \r\n  818: Contract: **OTR_DynamicStoryDirection, OTR_MetaBriefImagePromptGen AND\r\n  819: OTR_ShotLock** each tear down in a `finally` after their last LLM call, mirroring\r\n  820: the cascade (nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:377-387, 453-478):\r\n  821: `unload_llm_if_local_resident()`, a `*_unload_ok` stamp, loud logging, and an\r\n  822: ABORT before GPU image work if unloading raises. \"No local model was ever loaded\"\r\n  823: and \"teardown failed\" are DISTINCT receipts. Lazy imports throughout.\r\n  824: \r\n  825: ---\r\n  826: \r\n  827: ## 6. Dropdown / override semantics\r\n  828: \r\n  829: - The writer dropdown gains ONE entry: `dynamic_story`, appended CODE-SIDE as a\r\n  830:   sentinel next to `list_style_ids()` (the `ADD_CUSTOM` idiom,\r\n  831:   nodes/otr_video_director.py:35). `list_style_ids()` itself stays REGISTRY-ONLY.\r\n  832:   The placeholder-pack-file alternative is REJECTED (r1) -- and because no file is\r\n  833:   added, the registry sweep (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:329-336) needs no\r\n  834:   exemption.\r\n  835: - **The dropdown test changes in the same commit:**\r\n  836:   `test_choices_are_exactly_the_registry` asserts\r\n  837:   `choices == list(vs.list_style_ids())` (tests/test_visual_style_widget_3c.py:\r\n  838:   62-66). It becomes \"registry PLUS exactly one sentinel\" at the WRITER surface;\r\n  839:   the registry-only property is asserted on `list_style_ids()` itself.\r\n  840: - **Sentinel gate fix:** the writer's run() gate `resolve_visual_style(...)` raises\r\n  841:   on any id without a pack file (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3334-3339) --\r\n  842:   selecting `dynamic_story` today would kill the run BEFORE the story exists. The\r\n  843:   gate must special-case the sentinel; the stamp mechanics stay unchanged\r\n  844:   (:3651-3655).\r\n  845: - **Explicit named pack always wins, byte-identical:** when\r\n  846:   `meta.visual_style != \"dynamic_story\"` the direction node is a pure pass-through\r\n  847:   and every resolver behaves exactly as today. Absent/empty `visual_style` keeps\r\n  848:   resolving to `sci_fi_radio` (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:386-389). **Every new\r\n  849:   receipt/provenance field is DYNAMIC-LANE-ONLY** -- adding a field to image rows\r\n  850:   unconditionally would break the named-pack byte-identity baseline.\r\n  851: - **The sentinel VALUE is the only trigger.** Artifact presence never activates\r\n  852:   dynamic styling -- a stale `meta.visual_direction` under a named pack is inert.\r\n  853: - Precedence: (1) named pack -> current behavior, dynamic machinery inert;\r\n  854:   (2) `dynamic_story` -> artifact mandatory, fail-closed; (3) nothing -> production\r\n  855:   default pack. No env override, no silent fallback between lanes.\r\n  856: \r\n  857: ---\r\n  858: \r\n  859: ## 7. Failure, stale data, replay, and audit\r\n  860: \r\n  861: ### 7.1 Fail-closed matrix (enforced in `resolve_visual_direction`)\r\n  862: \r\n  863: With `meta.visual_style == \"dynamic_story\"`, ANY of the following aborts the\r\n  864: episode loudly (named error, never a fallback to a named pack):\r\n  865: \r\n  866: - `meta.visual_direction` absent or not a dict; `schema_version` not `vd-1`.\r\n  867: - `story_binding.episode_id` / `.freeze_timestamp` / `.freeze_verdict` differ from\r\n  868:   the live meta (a re-frozen or foreign ledger).\r\n  869: - REBUILT `DirectionSourceV1` hash differs from the bound `source_sha256` --\r\n  870:   authored story content changed after direction. (The DTO, not the raw arrays:\r\n  871:   post-freeze timing/voice mutations are EXPECTED and must not false-fail.)\r\n  872: - RECOMPUTED `semantic_sha256` or `artifact_sha256` mismatch (a checksum against\r\n  873:   corruption -- the digest lives inside the mutable ledger, so it is not\r\n  874:   tamper-proofing).\r\n  875: - Embedded `style_pack` fails v2 validation, or an `authored_fields` entry names a\r\n  876:   safety-base field.\r\n  877: - Any evidence ID fails to resolve; any `factual` quote is not a substring of its\r\n  878:   cited text; any authored key in the closed enum lacks a `field_evidence` entry.\r\n  879: - The `shots[]` set is not exactly the still-target set (a missing target, an\r\n  880:   unknown `line_id`, or a duplicate).\r\n  881: \r\n  882: Postures mirrored from: nodes/otr_image_director.py:428-456,\r\n  883: nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1053-1061, nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:367-375.\r\n  884: \r\n  885: ### 7.2 The ShotLock swallow\r\n  886: \r\n  887: ShotLock's prompt finisher wraps `finish_visual_prompt` in a bare\r\n  888: `except Exception: pass` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:626-636) -- on the dynamic lane\r\n  889: that would silently convert every 7.1 abort into an unstyled prompt. Dynamic-lane\r\n  890: contract: resolve ONCE, before the beat loop, OUTSIDE any fail-soft block, and pass\r\n  891: `style=` into the finisher. `VisualStyleError` and vd-1 validation errors must\r\n  892: PROPAGATE.\r\n  893: \r\n  894: ### 7.3 Story immutability\r\n  895: \r\n  896: Protection is the SOURCE-DTO COMPARISON (write-time re-hash refusing to stamp on\r\n  897: delta, 5.2 step 6; read-time re-hash, 7.1) -- NOT the merge ownership boundary,\r\n  898: which only controls disk copy-forward (nodes/production_ledger.py:1426-1459), and\r\n  899: NOT the freeze audit, which has already run.\r\n  900: \r\n  901: ### 7.4 Per-kind consumption matrix for `shots[]` (r3 antigravity M4 -- MANDATORY)\r\n  902: \r\n  903: The mood seam rev 3 cited (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1004-1008) lives\r\n  904: INSIDE `compose_still_word_prompt` and fires for `character_video` WORD CARDS only.\r\n  905: Appending the notes there would leave character-scene stills and beat stills --\r\n  906: the very shots the notes describe -- ignoring them entirely. That is dead LLM\r\n  907: output, which this design forbids. The consumption matrix is therefore explicit:\r\n  908: \r\n  909: | Prompt kind | Composer | `subject_note` | `mood` |\r\n  910: |---|---|---|---|\r\n  911: | scene still, character beat | `_compose_char_scene_prompt` (:1241-1366) | **YES** -- appended as a subject clause | **YES** |\r\n  912: | scene still, non-character beat | `compose_still_prompt` (nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:590) | **YES** | **YES** |\r\n  913: | still_word card | `compose_still_word_prompt` (:942-1013) | no (a word card has no subject) | **YES** -- overrides the derived mood adjective at :1004-1008 on character cards |\r\n  914: | portrait | portrait builders (:1148-1238) | no (per-CHARACTER, not per-line) | no |\r\n  915: | radio-host object | `build_radio_host_prompt` (:356-444) | no (per-EPISODE) | no |\r\n  916: | mesh fodder / background plate | (:1437-1496) | no (deliberately subject-free; `plate_look` is pack-level) | no |\r\n  917: | talking-head video prompt | ShotLock `finish_visual_prompt` | no in v1 (state explicitly) | no in v1 |\r\n  918: \r\n  919: Consequently `shots[]` rows exist ONLY for the still-target set (2.6), every row IS\r\n  920: consumed, and nothing authored is dead. Notes are ADDITIVE clauses: they can never\r\n  921: replace pack-level fields, are bounded (4.4), and are linted against the safety-base\r\n  922: `forbidden_terms` + the Python geometry vocabulary at validation time.\r\n  923: \r\n  924: Engine-safety continuity is structural: talking/mouth/motion/subject/typography\r\n  925: fields all come from the vetted base (2.4), so no per-episode LLM output can degrade\r\n  926: lip-sync or motion; `render_driver`'s `motion_registers` reads never vary with LLM\r\n  927: output.\r\n  928: \r\n  929: ### 7.5 Replay, reruns, and the reroll cut\r\n  930: \r\n  931: - **A canonical re-queue is NOT a replay** (1.6): the writer and cascade\r\n  932:   `IS_CHANGED` return `time.time()`. Replay is proven at the RESOLVER/CACHE seams in\r\n  933:   deterministic tests over a CAPTURED frozen ledger -- never as a live leg, and never\r\n  934:   with a test-only workflow or mutation node.\r\n  935: - The new node declares NO `IS_CHANGED`, so ComfyUI may serve it from cache when its\r\n  936:   input `script_json` is byte-identical. That is INTENTIONAL and desirable\r\n  937:   (immutable-per-source), and it is tested; it is reachable only when the upstream did\r\n  938:   not re-execute.\r\n  939: - Replay property that DOES hold: an unchanged STORED artifact composes byte-identical\r\n  940:   prompts -> dispatcher cache HITs; any PROMPT-AFFECTING change flows into\r\n  941:   `prompt_hash` -> new cache keys -> regeneration\r\n  942:   (nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:117-129). A change to `rationale` or a receipt\r\n  943:   alone does NOT invalidate the cache -- the key is the prompt hash.\r\n  944: - Reroll/revision is CUT from v1, and with it ARTIFACT HISTORY. The provenance digest\r\n  945:   identifies the artifact that authored the prompt for the CURRENT run; \"which\r\n  946:   historical artifact authored this cached pixel\" is explicitly not a v1 promise.\r\n  947: - REQUIRED: on the dynamic lane the Dispatcher writes `visual_direction_semantic_sha256`\r\n  948:   AND the composed prompt onto image rows **on BOTH the cache-miss and the cache-HIT\r\n  949:   path**. A hit CLONES the previous row (`fresh = dict(ref_row or {})`, :627-632), so an\r\n  950:   inherited digest would be STALE ATTRIBUTION. ShotLock does the same for its video\r\n  951:   `creative` sidecars, and on the dynamic lane the video section is persisted fail-loud\r\n  952:   rather than left on the wire.\r\n  953: \r\n  954: ### 7.6 Debug/audit walk (\"why does this shot look like this?\")\r\n  955: \r\n  956: 1. Rendered asset -> `ledger['images'].images[]` row (or\r\n  957:    `ledger['video'].shots[].creative`) -> composed `prompt` + `prompt_hash` +\r\n  958:    `visual_direction_semantic_sha256`.\r\n  959: 2. That digest -> the `meta.visual_direction` that authored the prompt.\r\n  960: 3. Prompt tail vocabulary -> `style_pack` fields (verbatim in the artifact) + the\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
