:    CastLock/ShotLock idiom (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:966-969). `done` is the standard\r\n  987:    opaque ordering STRING and ships UNWIRED, exactly as ShotLock's own `done` does\r\n  988:    today (`links: []`). `direction_report` also ships unwired -- and is therefore\r\n  989:    ALSO written to the log, so the observability claim is true either way. Zero\r\n  990:    widgets.\r\n  991: 2. **Registration in the LITERAL `_NODE_MODULES` dict in `__init__.py`** (:119-325;\r\n  992:    one tuple entry supplies BOTH the class mapping and the display name, written by\r\n  993:    the loader loop at :362-363). **NOT** via `nodes/_otr_class_registry.py`: the\r\n  994:    canonical-workflow contract test builds its node-class mappings by AST-parsing the\r\n  995:    literal `_NODE_MODULES` dict (tests/test_workflow_contract_validation.py:41) and\r\n  996:    never executes the class-registry merge (__init__.py:335-349) -- a registry-only\r\n  997:    node is INVISIBLE to the workflow gate.\r\n  998: 3. **Workflow JSON delta -- the literal record (same change as the code, CLAUDE.md\r\n  999:    section 0).** Counters: `last_node_id: 95 -> 96`, `last_link_id: 283 -> 284`.\r\n 1000:    REPOINT existing link ids; never renumber.\r\n 1001: \r\n 1002: ```json\r\n 1003: { \"id\": 96, \"type\": \"OTR_DynamicStoryDirection\",\r\n 1004:   \"pos\": [1060, 760], \"size\": [379.96875, 239.96875],\r\n 1005:   \"flags\": {}, \"order\": <topological -- after 62, before 89/90>, \"mode\": 0,\r\n 1006:   \"inputs\": [ { \"name\": \"script_json\", \"type\": \"STRING\", \"link\": 284 } ],\r\n 1007:   \"outputs\": [\r\n 1008:     { \"name\": \"patched_ledger_json\", \"type\": \"STRING\", \"links\": [252, 255],\r\n 1009:       \"slot_index\": 0 },\r\n 1010:     { \"name\": \"direction_report\", \"type\": \"STRING\", \"links\": [] },\r\n 1011:     { \"name\": \"done\", \"type\": \"STRING\", \"links\": [] } ],\r\n 1012:   \"properties\": { \"Node name for S&R\": \"OTR_DynamicStoryDirection\" },\r\n 1013:   \"widgets_values\": [] }\r\n 1014: ```\r\n 1015: \r\n 1016:    Links: ADD `[284, 62, 1, 96, 0, \"STRING\"]`; REPOINT\r\n 1017:    `[252, 96, 0, 90, 0, \"STRING\"]` and `[255, 96, 0, 89, 0, \"STRING\"]`.\r\n 1018:    Node 62 `outputs[1].links`: `[16, 231, 232, 233, 252, 255]` ->\r\n 1019:    `[16, 231, 232, 233, 284]`. Nodes 89/90 keep `inputs[0].link = 255 / 252` (the ids\r\n 1020:    do not change, only their SOURCE); no widget change anywhere.\r\n 1021:    **Re-baseline procedure, in order:** `OTR_WorkflowValidator`\r\n 1022:    (nodes/_otr_workflow_validator.py:183, `validate()` :394-480 -- note `_assert_stamp`\r\n 1023:    at :296-392 is the `semantic_master_hash` tripwire and `validate_anyway` can never\r\n 1024:    skip it, :400-408) -> JSON round-trip -> widget/`INPUT_TYPES` audit\r\n 1025:    (`_expected_slot_count`, :140-155) -> link/output-fan-out reconciliation -> master\r\n 1026:    hash stamp.\r\n 1027: 4. **`nodes/_otr_visual_direction.py`** (lazy; pydantic + stdlib): the typed models,\r\n 1028:    `DirectionSourceV1` + its per-pass views + the strict canonical hasher (shared by\r\n 1029:    writer and readers), evidence + quote resolution, geometry lint, pack assembly, the\r\n 1030:    fail-closed matrix, `resolve_visual_direction(ledger) -> ResolvedDirection`.\r\n 1031: 5. **`nodes/_otr_visual_direction_prompts.py`**: the P-A and P-B base prompts, the two\r\n 1032:    worked fixtures, and the vd-1 typed-repair directives (4.5).\r\n 1033: 6. **`nodes/_otr_visual_direction_base.py`**: the vetted safety base as a PYTHON\r\n 1034:    CONSTANT (D9 CLOSED -- a JSON file under `visual_styles/` would need a registry-sweep\r\n 1035:    exemption, nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:329-336, and could be picked up as a\r\n 1036:    selectable pack by accident).\r\n 1037: 7. **`nodes/_otr_structured_call.py`**: an ADDITIVE, backward-compatible attempt-event\r\n 1038:    sink parameter (4.5). No behavior change for existing callers.\r\n 1039: 8. **A provider-effective config + token-counting interface** (4.3) -- wherever Codex\r\n 1040:    lands it (`_otr_model_loader` is the natural home). Includes the must-fit guard.\r\n 1041: 9. **`nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py`**: code-side sentinel exposure for the dropdown\r\n 1042:    (registry unchanged); `visual_style_from_payload(dict)` funneling through\r\n 1043:    `_validate_row`; the `is_dynamic` flag; dynamic instances bypass `_STYLES`.\r\n 1044: 10. **`nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py`**: dynamic-lane look precedence in\r\n 1045:     `get_era_tail` / the palette reads (5.4).\r\n 1046: 11. **`nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py`**: sentinel-aware dropdown + run() gate (6).\r\n 1047: 12. **`nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py`**: `generate()` resolves via the ledger;\r\n 1048:     `derive_image_prompts` takes `style=` + `shots_by_line_id=` and threads them per the\r\n 1049:     7.4 matrix; `finally` LLM teardown.\r\n 1050: 13. **`nodes/otr_shot_lock.py`**: hoist style resolution above the beat loop (7.2);\r\n 1051:     `finally` LLM teardown; persist the video section fail-loud on the dynamic lane;\r\n 1052:     stamp the direction digest into the `creative` sidecars.\r\n 1053: 14. **`nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_driver.py`**: resolve once through the new seam\r\n 1054:     instead of `get_visual_style(meta)` (:1248); honor the dynamic look authority in the\r\n 1055:     brief-core branch (:2069-2080).\r\n 1056: 15. **`nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py`**: dynamic-lane `visual_direction_semantic_sha256`\r\n 1057:     + composed prompt on image rows, on BOTH the miss and the HIT path (7.5).\r\n 1058: \r\n 1059: ---\r\n 1060: \r\n 1061: ## 9. Test + live-smoke plan + sprint receipt\r\n 1062: \r\n 1063: ### 9.1 Unit (CPU, `OTR_TEST_MODE=1`, injected GenerateFn)\r\n 1064: \r\n 1065: Injection shape is `slot_fn(messages, *, temperature, max_new_tokens)` -- NOT\r\n 1066: ShotLock's `callable(prompt)->str` (4.2). Fakes modelled on\r\n 1067: tests/test_video_platform_aseam.py:401-500.\r\n 1068: \r\n 1069: 1. **Schema round-trip, PER PASS:** a valid draft validates; each required field's\r\n 1070:    absence fails named; `extra=\"forbid\"` rejects an unknown key at every depth; the\r\n 1071:    assembled pack goes through `_validate_row` verbatim; an `authored_fields` entry\r\n 1072:    naming a safety-base field fails.\r\n 1073: 2. **No-silent-clamp:** an over-long `subject_note` / `era_tail` reaches TYPED REPAIR\r\n 1074:    (via `post_validator`) and is NEVER truncated-and-accepted. This test exists\r\n 1075:    specifically to pin the 2.1 decision against\r\n 1076:    `_clamp_overlong_strings` (nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:422-434).\r\n 1077: 3. **Wrong-depth battery, PER PASS** (the PBUG-20260712-02/-03 class): P-A with\r\n 1078:    `evidence` nested inside a `look` value, or `field_evidence` nested inside `motifs`;\r\n 1079:    P-B with `shots` nested inside a row, a singular `shot` alias, a numbered\r\n 1080:    `era_tail_2`. Each must either be deterministically relocated (unique destination\r\n 1081:    ONLY, and the factory must pass the COMPLETE contract before returning) or advance\r\n 1082:    the LLM repair rung -- never be silently accepted.\r\n 1083: 4. **Repair-ladder accounting:** a syntax failure runs the structural rung; a schema or\r\n 1084:    post-validation failure goes STRAIGHT to typed repair; exhaustion raises\r\n 1085:    `StructuredCallFailedError` and the episode aborts. The `attempt_journal` records\r\n 1086:    every rung with its reason.\r\n 1087: 5. **Context preflight:** a fixture whose P-A prompt exceeds `context_cap -\r\n 1088:    reserve - repair_envelope` RAISES before any generation, naming the real numbers; a\r\n 1089:    schema-maximum P-B batch that cannot fit RAISES before P-A is even run.\r\n 1090: 6. **Evidence + quote:** an unresolvable id fails; a `factual` entry whose quote is not\r\n 1091:    a substring of the cited text fails; an id valid in the DTO but absent from the\r\n 1092:    citing pass's VIEW fails.\r\n 1093: 7. **Fail-closed matrix:** one test per row of 7.1 -- all raise; NONE fall back to a\r\n 1094:    named pack.\r\n 1095: 8. **Inert-path byte-identity, PARAMETERIZED over every registered pack +\r\n 1096:    absent/default style:** serialized ledger, composed prompts, prompt_hashes and\r\n 1097:    dispatcher request keys are byte-identical before vs after the feature.\r\n 1098:    **Capture those four baselines as committed fixtures BEFORE any code lands** -- once\r\n 1099:    the code changes there is no immutable \"before\".\r\n 1100: 9. **Channel isolation:** run the SAME mocked story twice, changing ONLY\r\n 1101:    `visual_style` (`sci_fi_radio` vs `dynamic_story`). Every pre-freeze story-model\r\n 1102:    message must be byte-identical; only the post-freeze direction lane and the selector\r\n 1103:    receipt may differ. This proves the sentinel never leaks into the story channel.\r\n 1104: 10. **Source-DTO stability:** ShotLock's timing overlay + CastLock's voice-preset\r\n 1105:     assignment do NOT change `source_sha256`; a one-word text edit DOES.\r\n 1106: 11. **Merge survival, SPLIT in two:** (a) in-memory stamping under `OTR_TEST_MODE=1`\r\n 1107:     (where `stamp_durable` skips the disk write, nodes/production_ledger.py:408-452);\r\n 1108:     (b) a real `Ledger.save()` merge in an isolated tmpdir asserting restoration from\r\n 1109:     disk (mirror of tests/test_ledger_merge_ownership.py).\r\n 1110: 12. **Story immutability:** a mutating fake is refused; `source_recheck` is not\r\n 1111:     `clean`.\r\n 1112: 13. **Hash determinism:** same fixture + same injected output => identical\r\n 1113:     `semantic_sha256`; `created_utc` / receipt variation changes ONLY the envelope hash.\r\n 1114:     (A property of the STORED artifact, not of the LLM: the local lane hardcodes\r\n 1115:     `do_sample=True` with no seed, nodes/_otr_model_loader.py:1122-1129, so\r\n 1116:     re-derivation is NOT reproducible.)\r\n 1117: 14. **Per-kind consumption matrix (7.4):** for each kind, assert the note/mood clause\r\n 1118:     IS or IS NOT present in the composed prompt, exactly as the matrix says; assert\r\n 1119:     every `shots[]` row is consumed by at least one prompt; assert the `shots[]` set\r\n 1120:     equals the still-target set.\r\n 1121: 15. **Look authority:** parameterized `get_era_tail` / palette tests asserting the\r\n 1122:     pack-authored tail wins verbatim and the brief is IGNORED when `is_dynamic` -- in\r\n 1123:     the still lane AND in render_driver's brief-core branch.\r\n 1124: 16. **Consumer propagation:** with dynamic selected and a broken artifact, MetaBrief,\r\n 1125:     ShotLock AND render_driver all RAISE (do not swallow, do not fall back).\r\n 1126: 17. **Teardown:** each of the three LLM-touching post-freeze nodes unloads in `finally`;\r\n 1127:     a teardown failure RAISES and never proceeds to GPU work.\r\n 1128: 18. **Dispatcher provenance:** on the dynamic lane, a cache HIT row carries the CURRENT\r\n 1129:     digest and prompt -- not the cloned row's (pins :627-632); on a named pack, image\r\n 1130:     rows are byte-identical to the pre-feature baseline (no new fields).\r\n 1131: 19. **Replay at the seam** (not live): a captured frozen ledger + an unchanged artifact\r\n 1132:     recomposes byte-identical prompts and identical dispatcher request keys.\r\n 1133: 20. **Topology test:** the canonical JSON wires `62:1 -> 96:0 -> {89:0, 90:0}`; node 62's\r\n 1134:     remaining fan-out is exactly `[16, 231, 232, 233, 284]`;\r\n 1135:     `OTR_DynamicStoryDirection` is in the literal `_NODE_MODULES`.\r\n 1136: 21. **Look-QA rubric fixtures:** a small multi-genre fixture set (noir / western /\r\n 1137:     sci-fi source DTOs) with an operator rubric -- specificity, palette/medium coherence,\r\n 1138:     recurring identity, talking-lane safety, measurable difference from the fixed-pack\r\n 1139:     control. Schema validity alone does not prove the direction is any good.\r\n 1140: \r\n 1141: Suite discipline: full Windows regression + Bug Bible after every code chunk (CLAUDE.md\r\n 1142: section 3). The conftest hard-fails the session on ANY new failed nodeid\r\n 1143: (tests/conftest.py:219-286), so this is a real gate. Three-File Contract for any new bug\r\n 1144: class.\r\n 1145: \r\n 1146: **Tests that BREAK and must change in the same commit:**\r\n 1147: `tests/test_visual_style_widget_3c.py:62-66` (choices == registry -> registry +\r\n 1148: sentinel); `tests/test_google_video_sfx_workflow.py:41` (`last_link_id == 283` -> 284).\r\n 1149: **Generic gates that must stay green:** `tests/test_workflow_graph_integrity_guards.py`\r\n 1150: (widget-vector drift; link source-slot bounds; **output-link reconciliation** -- if the\r\n 1151: delta repoints 252/255 in `links[]` but leaves them in `62.outputs[1].links`, this is\r\n 1152: what fires); `tests/test_workflow_live_passes_validator.py:41-47`;\r\n 1153: `tests/test_core.py:410-415` (id ceilings); `tests/test_workflow_link_target_indexes.py`;\r\n 1154: `tests/test_full_workflow_v2_audio_wiring.py:149, 220-232` (the audio trio + CastLock stay\r\n 1155: on the raw freeze outputs).\r\n 1156: **Caveat:** the contract test runs with `strict_unknown_types=False`, so a class that\r\n 1157: fails to IMPORT in the bare test env is silently SKIPPED there. A green contract test is\r\n 1158: NOT proof the node registered -- the topology test (item 20) is.\r\n 1159: \r\n 1160: ### 9.2 Model-diversity qualification ladder (Lesson 6)\r\n 1161: \r\n 1162: Both slots default to Mistral-Nemo (`DEFAULT_LLM`, nodes/_otr_model_catalog.py:32). A\r\n 1163: prompt proven on one family is not qualified.\r\n 1164: \r\n 1165: 1. unit fixtures + full Windows suite + Bug Bible;\r\n 1166: 2. canonical 30-word end-to-end on **two local families** --\r\n 1167:    `mistralai/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407` and `google/gemma-4-E4B-it [LOCAL HF]` (the\r\n 1168:    family behind PBUG-20260712-02 and -03, i.e. the one that demonstrably fails\r\n 1169:    DIFFERENTLY) -- plus **one configured cloud/frontier creative lane**. The cloud lane\r\n 1170:    is DECLARED before the run, with its concrete model id, its auth path (OpenRouter is\r\n 1171:    key-gated, nodes/_otr_openrouter_backend.py:272), whether constrained generation is\r\n 1172:    available on it (4.3 -- Google has NO branch today), and its rate policy. It is never\r\n 1173:    silently skipped.\r\n 1174: 3. the same three pairings at 120 words;\r\n 1175: 4. only then any 720-word qualification / bake-off.\r\n 1176: \r\n 1177: Record per leg: concrete model label, provider, slot, prompt_version, repair-rung counts\r\n 1178: from the attempt journal, measured token budget, ledger path, episode asset path,\r\n 1179: published asset path.\r\n 1180: \r\n 1181: ### 9.3 Live smoke (5080, headless :8000, reset per CLAUDE.md section 4)\r\n 1182: \r\n 1183: Every leg loads the REAL `workflows/otr_canonical.json`.\r\n 1184: \r\n 1185: 1. **Control leg:** 30-word episode, `visual_style=\"sci_fi_radio\"` -- prompts byte-match\r\n 1186:    the committed pre-feature baseline (9.1 item 8).\r\n 1187: 2. **Dynamic legs:** the 9.2 ladder. Each asserts: the artifact is on the DISK ledger\r\n 1188:    with full receipts; the attempt journal shows the rungs; still prompts carry the\r\n 1189:    authored vocabulary AND the per-line notes per the 7.4 matrix; **no local LLM is\r\n 1190:    resident when the Dispatcher's GPU work begins** (which requires MetaBrief's and\r\n 1191:    ShotLock's teardown too, 5.5); assets exist at `otr\\episodes\\<ep>\\` (Test-Path);\r\n 1192:    `obs_publish OK` **AND** the final file exists under `otr\\obs\\` (Lesson 7 --\r\n 1193:    `obs_publish OK` alone is not proof).\r\n 1194: 3. **Stale-source and replay:** NOT live legs (1.6, 7.5) -- proven deterministically over\r\n 1195:    a captured frozen ledger.\r\n 1196: \r\n 1197: Any failure in a LIVE run (smoke, soak, or published episode) gets an append-only\r\n 1198: `PBUG-<YYYYMMDD>-<NN>` entry in docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md using the template at :15-26\r\n 1199: (surfaced / symptom / root cause / fix / verify idea / bible-worthy / confidence /\r\n 1200: status). Dev-only catches are fixed and tested but NOT logged. Bible promotion happens at\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
