sed through.\r\n  575:       schema\r\n  576:         A pydantic model class. The LLM response is parsed and\r\n  577:         validated against it; the validated instance is returned.\r\n  578:       slot_fn\r\n  579:         The LLM generate callable. Signature in this codebase:\r\n  580:         `slot_fn(messages, *, temperature, max_new_tokens[, stop])\r\n  581:         -> str`.\r\n  582:       base_temperature\r\n  583:         Attempt 1 temperature.\r\n  584:       structural_retry_temperature\r\n  585:         Attempt 2 temperature. MUST be strictly lower than\r\n  586:         `base_temperature` (the 2B principle -- the structural retry\r\n  587:         lowers entropy, it does not raise it). The invariant is\r\n  588:         asserted at entry and fails loud if violated.\r\n  589:       repair_prompt_factory\r\n  590:         Callable that builds the Attempt 3 typed-repair prompt from the\r\n  591:         failed output + the validation error. `None` selects\r\n  592:         `default_repair_prompt_factory`. A factory may instead return a\r\n  593:         finished `schema` instance, which is accepted directly with no\r\n  594:         LLM repair call (see `RepairPromptFactory`). The built repair\r\n  595:         messages are cached for one syntax-only retry if budget remains.\r\n  596:       post_validator\r\n  597:         Optional content check run on every schema-valid instance,\r\n  598:         `post_validator(instance) -> str | None`. It returns an error\r\n  599:         string to REJECT the instance (a content failure pydantic\r\n  600:         cannot see -- e.g. a voice preset outside the runtime pool, a\r\n  601:         news brief below the key-term floor, a speaker outside the\r\n  602:         locked cast) or `None` to ACCEPT it. A rejection is raised as\r\n  603:         `PostValidationError` and advances the ladder exactly like a\r\n  604:         schema failure. Mirrors the `extra_check` idiom already used by\r\n  605:         `_otr_outline._run_call_with_retry`. `None` disables the check.\r\n  606:       max_new_tokens\r\n  607:         Token budget passed to `slot_fn` on every attempt. Structured\r\n  608:         passes vary widely -- a story-brief reflection needs ~160, a\r\n  609:         cast-contract audit ~2000, a script-doctor pass ~3500 -- so the\r\n  610:         caller sets its own budget. Defaults to\r\n  611:         `_STRUCTURED_MAX_NEW_TOKENS` (512) for a small JSON object.\r\n  612:       max_attempts\r\n  613:         Caps the ladder (default 3).\r\n  614:       helper_name\r\n  615:         Short string for logging / slot attribution.\r\n  616: \r\n  617:     The ladder (stops at the first schema-valid result that also\r\n  618:     clears `post_validator`; only `json.JSONDecodeError`,\r\n  619:     `pydantic.ValidationError`, and `PostValidationError` are recoverable\r\n  620:     -- a plain `ValueError` propagates):\r\n  621:       Attempt 1: `slot_fn` at `base_temperature`.\r\n  622:       Structural retry: SAME prompt at `structural_retry_temperature`\r\n  623:                  (lower) -- run ONLY when the prior failure was a\r\n  624:                  `json.JSONDecodeError` (malformed JSON a calmer re-prompt\r\n  625:                  may fix). A `ValidationError` / `PostValidationError`\r\n  626:                  SKIPS this rung (a re-prompt re-emits the same bad shape\r\n  627:                  and only burns tokens) and goes straight to typed repair.\r\n  628:       Typed repair: `repair_prompt_factory` either builds a repair prompt\r\n  629:                  (run at the static low temperature `_REPAIR_TEMPERATURE`)\r\n  630:                  or hands back a finished `schema` instance, returned\r\n  631:                  directly with no LLM call.\r\n  632:       Repair syntax retry: if the typed repair returned non-decodable JSON\r\n  633:                  and budget remains, retry its exact cached prompt once at\r\n  634:                  a bounded temperature above the static repair floor. This\r\n  635:                  does not run for schema or content rejection.\r\n  636:     \"\"\"\r\n  637:     # --- Invariant: structural retry must LOWER temperature (2B). ---\r\n  638:     # Fail loud at entry. A structural retry at >= base temperature is\r\n  639:     # a configuration bug, not a recoverable runtime state.\r\n  640:     if not structural_retry_temperature < base_temperature:\r\n  641:         raise ValueError(\r\n  642:             f\"[OTR_StructuredCall] '{helper_name}': \"\r\n  643:             f\"structural_retry_temperature ({structural_retry_temperature}) \"\r\n  644:             f\"must be STRICTLY LOWER than base_temperature \"\r\n  645:             f\"({base_temperature}). Raising entropy during JSON-schema \"\r\n  646:             \"repair encourages more structural hallucination, not less; \"\r\n  647:             \"the structural retry lowers temperature.\"\r\n  648:         )\r\n  649: \r\n  650:     if max_attempts < 1:\r\n  651:         raise ValueError(\r\n  652:             f\"[OTR_StructuredCall] '{helper_name}': max_attempts must be \"\r\n  653:             f\">= 1, got {max_attempts}\"\r\n  654:         )\r\n  655: \r\n  656:     factory: RepairPromptFactory = (\r\n  657:         repair_prompt_factory\r\n  658:         if repair_prompt_factory is not None\r\n  659:         else default_repair_prompt_factory\r\n  660:     )\r\n  661: \r\n  662:     base_messages = _prompt_to_messages(prompt)\r\n  663:     last_error: Optional[BaseException] = None\r\n  664:     last_raw: str = \"\"\r\n  665:     attempts_run = 0\r\n  666:     repair_messages: Any = None\r\n  667: \r\n  668:     # --- Attempt 1: base temperature. ---\r\n  669:     if attempts_run < max_attempts:\r\n  670:         attempts_run += 1\r\n  671:         log.info(\r\n  672:             \"[OTR_StructuredCall] '%s' attempt %d/%d: base call at \"\r\n  673:             \"temperature=%.3f\",\r\n  674:             helper_name, attempts_run, max_attempts, base_temperature,\r\n  675:         )\r\n  676:         try:\r\n  677:             last_raw = _invoke_slot(\r\n  678:                 slot_fn, base_messages,\r\n  679:                 temperature=base_temperature,\r\n  680:                 max_new_tokens=max_new_tokens,\r\n  681:             )\r\n  682:             return _parse_and_validate(last_raw, schema, post_validator)\r\n  683:         except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValidationError, PostValidationError) as exc:\r\n  684:             last_error = exc\r\n  685:             log.warning(\r\n  686:                 \"[OTR_StructuredCall] '%s' attempt %d failed: %s | raw \"\r\n  687:                 \"head: %s\", helper_name, attempts_run, exc,\r\n  688:                 _raw_head(last_raw),\r\n  689:             )\r\n  690: \r\n  691:     # --- Structural retry: SAME prompt, lower temperature -- ONLY for a JSON\r\n  692:     # SYNTAX failure. A re-prompt at lower temperature can shake loose a\r\n  693:     # parseable object when the model emitted malformed JSON. It does NOT help a\r\n  694:     # ValidationError / PostValidationError (the JSON parsed; the SHAPE or\r\n  695:     # CONTENT is wrong) -- a re-prompt just re-emits the same shape, burning a\r\n  696:     # credit-billed call (the 2026-06-25 Opus normalize_length exhaustion: the\r\n  697:     # structural rung never helped, it only spent tokens). So on a non-syntax\r\n  698:     # failure skip straight to the typed repair; spend the structural retry only\r\n  699:     # on json.JSONDecodeError. attempts_run advances ONLY when this branch runs.\r\n  700:     if attempts_run < max_attempts and isinstance(last_error, json.JSONDecodeError):\r\n  701:         attempts_run += 1\r\n  702:         log.info(\r\n  703:             \"[OTR_StructuredCall] '%s' attempt %d/%d: structural retry at \"\r\n  704:             \"temperature=%.3f (lowered from %.3f)\",\r\n  705:             helper_name, attempts_run, max_attempts,\r\n  706:             structural_retry_temperature, base_temperature,\r\n  707:         )\r\n  708:         try:\r\n  709:             last_raw = _invoke_slot(\r\n  710:                 slot_fn, base_messages,\r\n  711:                 temperature=structural_retry_temperature,\r\n  712:                 max_new_tokens=max_new_tokens,\r\n  713:             )\r\n  714:             return _parse_and_validate(last_raw, schema, post_validator)\r\n  715:         except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValidationError, PostValidationError) as exc:\r\n  716:             last_error = exc\r\n  717:             log.warning(\r\n  718:                 \"[OTR_StructuredCall] '%s' attempt %d failed: %s | raw \"\r\n  719:                 \"head: %s\", helper_name, attempts_run, exc,\r\n  720:                 _raw_head(last_raw),\r\n  721:             )\r\n  722: \r\n  723:     # --- Typed repair at a static low temperature (the final rung). ---\r\n  724:     if attempts_run < max_attempts:\r\n  725:         attempts_run += 1\r\n  726:         log.info(\r\n  727:             \"[OTR_StructuredCall] '%s' attempt %d/%d: typed repair at \"\r\n  728:             \"temperature=%.3f\",\r\n  729:             helper_name, attempts_run, max_attempts, _REPAIR_TEMPERATURE,\r\n  730:         )\r\n  731:         try:\r\n  732:             repair_error: BaseException = (\r\n  733:                 last_error\r\n  734:                 if last_error is not None\r\n  735:                 else ValueError(\"no prior error captured\")\r\n  736:             )\r\n  737:             repair_prompt = factory(\r\n  738:                 original_prompt=prompt,\r\n  739:                 failed_output=last_raw,\r\n  740:                 error=repair_error,\r\n  741:             )\r\n  742:             # A typed repair factory MAY resolve the failure itself --\r\n  743:             # e.g. cast_membership_repair remapping a phantom speaker to\r\n  744:             # a locked-cast member via Levenshtein -- and hand back a\r\n  745:             # finished `schema` instance instead of a repair prompt.\r\n  746:             # Accept it directly: no LLM repair call is made. The\r\n  747:             # instance still passes through post_validator so a\r\n  748:             # deterministic \"fix\" that is itself content-invalid fails\r\n  749:             # the ladder loudly rather than slipping through.\r\n  750:             if isinstance(repair_prompt, schema):\r\n  751:                 if post_validator is not None:\r\n  752:                     content_error = post_validator(repair_prompt)\r\n  753:                     if content_error is not None:\r\n  754:                         raise PostValidationError(content_error)\r\n  755:                 log.info(\r\n  756:                     \"[OTR_StructuredCall] '%s' attempt %d: repair factory \"\r\n  757:                     \"resolved the failure deterministically; no LLM \"\r\n  758:                     \"repair call made\",\r\n  759:                     helper_name, attempts_run,\r\n  760:                 )\r\n  761:                 return repair_prompt\r\n  762:             repair_messages = _prompt_to_messages(repair_prompt)\r\n  763:             last_raw = _invoke_slot(\r\n  764:                 slot_fn, repair_messages,\r\n  765:                 temperature=_REPAIR_TEMPERATURE,\r\n  766:                 max_new_tokens=max_new_tokens,\r\n  767:             )\r\n  768:             return _parse_and_validate(last_raw, schema, post_validator)\r\n  769:         except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValidationError, PostValidationError) as exc:\r\n  770:             last_error = exc\r\n  771:             log.warning(\r\n  772:                 \"[OTR_StructuredCall] '%s' attempt %d (repair) failed: \"\r\n  773:                 \"%s | raw head: %s\",\r\n  774:                 helper_name, attempts_run, exc, _raw_head(last_raw),\r\n  775:             )\r\n  776: \r\n  777:     # A semantic/schema failure on the base call skips the structural rung,\r\n  778:     # so typed repair can be attempt