{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r1\\\\input.md';\"'$lines=Get-Content $p;for($n=0;$n -lt 120;$n++){'\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f (\"'$n+1),$lines[$n]}'","aggregated_output":"    1: # dynamic_story -- Story-Derived Visual Direction: Scoped Design (docs-only)\r\n    2: \r\n    3: Date: 2026-07-12\r\n    4: Author: Claude (Cowork), docs-only architecture owner for this feature.\r\n    5: Implementation owner: Codex (all code, tests, registries, prompts, workflow JSON).\r\n    6: Status: DESIGN ONLY. Nothing in this document is implemented. No code, test,\r\n    7: prompt, registry, or workflows/otr_canonical.json change accompanies it.\r\n    8: \r\n    9: Scope contract honored here:\r\n   10: \r\n   11: - One additional option (`dynamic_story`) in the EXISTING visual-style dropdown.\r\n   12: - When selected, an LLM reads the final accepted/frozen story and authors an\r\n   13:   episode-specific, evidence-bound `visual_direction` artifact that every\r\n   14:   downstream visual composer consumes.\r\n   15: - An explicit user-selected named visual pack keeps current behavior,\r\n   16:   byte-identical, and always wins. `dynamic_story` is opt-in per episode.\r\n   17: \r\n   18: Every code claim below is grounded `file:line` against the real Windows repo at\r\n   19: the time of writing (v2.0-alpha working tree, 2026-07-12).\r\n   20: \r\n   21: ---\r\n   22: \r\n   23: ## 1. Grounded current dataflow (what exists today)\r\n   24: \r\n   25: ### 1.1 The visual-style selector and its one stamping point\r\n   26: \r\n   27: - The dropdown lives on OTR_LedgerScriptWriter: choices come LIVE from the\r\n   28:   visual-style pack registry (`list_style_ids()`) at INPUT_TYPES\r\n   29:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:2871-2889), default `sci_fi_radio`.\r\n   30: - The id is gated fail-loud at the top of `run()` beside the source-bank gate:\r\n   31:   `_otr_visual_styles.resolve_visual_style(visual_style)` -- unknown id raises\r\n   32:   `UnknownVisualStyleError` before ANY story work\r\n   33:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3334-3339).\r\n   34: - The ONE authoritative stamp: `meta[\"visual_style\"] = resolved[\"visual_style\"]`\r\n   35:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3651-3655). The comment there is the\r\n   36:   threading law: \"every downstream visual composer reads meta['visual_style']\r\n   37:   via get_visual_style(meta) off the serialized ledger\".\r\n   38: - Channel separation is explicit and load-bearing: `meta.style` is the STORY\r\n   39:   grammar slug (from the story contract), `meta.visual_style` is the visual\r\n   40:   prompt-pack selector; the two are never crossed\r\n   41:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:216-222, 2249-2261).\r\n   42: \r\n   43: ### 1.2 The pack registry (the resolution seam dynamic_story must enter through)\r\n   44: \r\n   45: - Packs are JSON files under `nodes/visual_styles/<style_id>.json`; the module\r\n   46:   is pure behavior, lazy, fail-loud (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:3-13, 50).\r\n   47: - `DEFAULT_STYLE_ID = \"sci_fi_radio\"` (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:53).\r\n   48: - Schema v2 is a FIXED field inventory: v1 fields (style_id, label, the four\r\n   49:   tails, forbidden_terms, ...) + 11 required look/subject strings + 4 dict\r\n   50:   fields with exact key sets (open_subjects, motion_registers,\r\n   51:   still_word_typography, still_word_backdrop)\r\n   52:   (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:60-102). Validation is strict: template\r\n   53:   placeholder rules, mouth-vocabulary contract, 240-char motion budget,\r\n   54:   forbidden-terms lint (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:109-123, 184+).\r\n   55: - Resolution: `resolve_visual_style(style_id)` -- unknown id = hard error, no\r\n   56:   fallback (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:367-375); `get_visual_style(meta)` --\r\n   57:   absent/empty `meta[\"visual_style\"]` = production default; PRESENT-but-unknown\r\n   58:   fails LOUD (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:378-390).\r\n   59: - The geometry-vs-look law (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:7-9): packs own ONLY\r\n   60:   look/subject vocabulary; framing/headroom/mouth-safety GEOMETRY stays in\r\n   61:   Python. `dynamic_story` must obey the same law -- the LLM authors LOOK, never\r\n   62:   geometry.\r\n   63: \r\n   64: ### 1.3 The story freeze boundary (what \"final accepted story\" means)\r\n   65: \r\n   66: - OTR_LedgerScriptWriter -> OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade; Phase 10 runs the\r\n   67:   deterministic gap audit and, on success, stamps\r\n   68:   `meta.cleanup_locked = True`, `meta.freeze_timestamp` (ISO-8601 UTC), and\r\n   69:   `meta.freeze_verdict = frozen_clean | frozen_with_warns`\r\n   70:   (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:758-819, stamps at 806-811). Critical gaps raise\r\n   71:   `FreezeAssertionError` and stamp `needs_full_rerun`\r\n   72:   (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:787-795).\r\n   73: - Post-freeze extension is an established pattern, not a violation: OTR_CastLock\r\n   74:   assigns voice presets AFTER the freeze (acknowledged inside the freeze audit\r\n   75:   itself, nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:493-502), and OTR_ShotLock stamps a whole\r\n   76:   `ledger['video']` section + `meta.video_revision` onto the frozen ledger\r\n   77:   (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1104-1131). Freeze locks story CONTENT (lines / cast\r\n   78:   / beats), not the ledger's ability to gain new namespaced sections.\r\n   79: \r\n   80: ### 1.4 Canonical wiring (workflows/otr_canonical.json, live graph)\r\n   81: \r\n   82: Grounded by walking `nodes[]`/`links[]` of the real file (litegraph schema,\r\n   83: single-line JSON; node ids below are the live ids):\r\n   84: \r\n   85: - Writer (node 1) `script_json` -> link 230 -> FreezeCascade (node 62).\r\n   86:   The writer's `visual_style` widget is combined widget slot 24\r\n   87:   (`widgets_values[24] == \"sci_fi_radio\"` in the canonical file; input name\r\n   88:   `visual_style` at in[24]).\r\n   89: - FreezeCascade out[1] `script_json` -> link 255 -> OTR_MetaBriefImagePromptGen\r\n   90:   (node 89) in[0], and -> link 252 -> OTR_ShotLock (node 90) in[0].\r\n   91: - OTR_VideoDirector (node 87) `video_policy_json` -> link 270 ->\r\n   92:   OTR_ImageDirector (node 88) in[0], and -> link 251 -> ShotLock in[2].\r\n   93: - ImageDirector `image_policy_json` -> link 254 -> MetaBrief in[1], and ->\r\n   94:   link 257 -> OTR_ImageGenDispatcher (node 91) in[1].\r\n   95: - MetaBrief out[0] `image_prompts_json` -> link 258 -> Dispatcher in[2].\r\n   96: - ShotLock out[0] `patched_ledger_json` -> link 256 -> Dispatcher in[0];\r\n   97:   ShotLock out[4] `episode_id` -> link 268 -> Dispatcher in[4].\r\n   98: - OTR_EpisodeAssembler (node 7) out[3] `audio_done` -> link 253 -> ShotLock\r\n   99:   in[1] and -> link 259 -> Dispatcher gate_in.\r\n  100: - Dispatcher out[0] -> link 260 -> OTR_VideoRenderBatch (node 92) in[0];\r\n  101:   Dispatcher out[1] `image_done` -> link 267 -> RenderBatch in[2].\r\n  102: \r\n  103: So the frozen ledger fans out on FreezeCascade out[1]; every visual composer\r\n  104: sees `meta.visual_style` on that wire.\r\n  105: \r\n  106: ### 1.5 Where the style is actually consumed (resolve-once contract)\r\n  107: \r\n  108: - Image prompts: `derive_image_prompts` resolves the style ONCE at entry --\r\n  109:   `_vstyle = _resolve_style(meta)` -- and threads it down; \"an unknown\r\n  110:   meta['visual_style'] stops the episode HERE, before any prompt is composed\"\r\n  111:   (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1601-1609). Consumers of the threaded\r\n  112:   pack include: portrait fallback + LLM instruction builders\r\n  113:   (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1148-1238), beat-aware character scene\r\n  114:   builder (:1241-1366), radio-host prompts (`build_radio_host_prompt`,\r\n  115:   :356-444), mesh fodder + background plate (:1437-1496), still_word cards\r\n  116:   (`compose_still_word_prompt`, :942-1013), and the aspect anchors\r\n  117:   (`_style_anchor_for_aspect`, :171-188).\r\n  118: - Video prompts: ShotLock's M4 creative derivation finishes every talking-head\r\n  119:   prompt through `finish_visual_prompt(meta, text_prompt)`\r\n  120:   (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:626-636); the helper family\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
