    the byte-identical ERA_TAIL_DEFAULT fallback -- production composers\r\n  354:     always pass ``style`` (AST-pinned).\r\n  355: \r\n  356:     ``profile=\"full\"`` (default; every pre-still-spine call site, behavior\r\n  357:     unchanged) ports the legacy ``_resolve_era_tail`` precedence (Sprint\r\n  358:     8.7): ``atmosphere_line`` -> ``visual_palette`` (top 3) -> v1\r\n  359:     lighting+atmosphere (:func:`get_story_brief_lighting`) -> the\r\n  360:     :data:`ERA_TAIL_DEFAULT` constant. v2 fields come through the canonical\r\n  361:     brief reader; every failure path degrades, fail-soft.\r\n  362: \r\n  363:     ``profile=\"still\"`` (still-spine ST-1): the TRIMMED tail for still-image\r\n  364:     prompts -- atmosphere line + palette top-2 + lighting top-2, capped at\r\n  365:     ~120 chars on a word boundary. Stills carry their subject up front; the\r\n  366:     full tail diet would push FLUX toward atmosphere soup. The per-episode\r\n  367:     palette color (e.g. Mars = red) comes through HERE by design -- the\r\n  368:     still profile trims the tail, never deletes it.\r\n  369:     \"\"\"\r\n  370:     _era_default = style.era_tail if style is not None else ERA_TAIL_DEFAULT\r\n  371:     atmosphere_line = \"\"\r\n  372:     palette: list[str] = []\r\n  373:     try:\r\n  374:         try:\r\n  375:             from ._otr_brief_reader import _read_brief_field  # type: ignore\r\n  376:         except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- flat test imports\r\n  377:             from _otr_brief_reader import _read_brief_field  # type: ignore\r\n  378:         raw_line = _read_brief_field(meta, \"atmosphere_line\", default=\"\")\r\n  379:         if isinstance(raw_line, str):\r\n  380:             atmosphere_line = raw_line.strip()\r\n  586:     \"full head and shoulders with clear headroom inside frame, face unobstructed, \"\r\n  587:     \"balanced landscape composition\")\r\n  588: \r\n  589: \r\n  590: def compose_still_prompt(meta: Any, *, kind: str, role: str = \"\",\r\n  591:                          beat_id: str = \"\", char_entry: Any = None,\r\n  592:                          style: Any = None) -> str:\r\n  593:     \"\"\"ONE still-image prompt in the legacy 5-layer order: subject /\r\n  594:     setting top-2 / framing hint / TRIMMED era tail (still profile) /\r\n  595:     style tail. Scene kinds append the :data:`NO_TEXT_CLAUSE` (a render\r\n  596:     constraint stills must carry; portraits never need it).\r\n  597: \r\n  598:     ``kind``: ``\"portrait\"`` leads with the character's own description\r\n  599:     (``portrait_prompt`` -> ``appearance`` -> ``character_description`` on\r\n  600:     ``char_entry``); ``\"scene_character\"`` (BUG 1, 2026-06-20) ALSO leads with\r\n  601:     the character description but composes a WIDE 16:9 medium shot (the landscape\r\n  602:     still-only character beat -- still_flat/still_pan/ltx_video) and DROPS the\r\n  603:     radio-booth tail; every other scene kind (``scene_open`` / ``scene_beat``)\r\n  604:     leads with :func:`get_open_subject` (``synthetic`` = kind==\"scene_open\"\r\n  605:     -- the b000 opening-music beat is the synthetic open). Never returns\r\n  606:     empty (the subject layer always exists). Stage 3: the tails come from\r\n  607:     the resolved visual-style pack (``style`` param, or a fail-loud\r\n  608:     ``get_visual_style(meta)`` when None -- a composer ENTRY seam); the\r\n  609:     broadcast tail additionally gates on ``pack.allow_radio_tails``. A\r\n  610:     style-resolution error RAISES (no-fallback law).\r\n  611:     \"\"\"\r\n  612:     _style = _resolve_style(meta, style)\r\n  613:     is_portrait = (kind == \"portrait\")\r\n  614:     is_char_scene = (kind == \"scene_character\")\r\n  615:     if is_portrait or is_char_scene:\r\n  616:         # Both lead with the CHARACTER's own description; scene_character just\r\n  617:         # frames them in a wide environment instead of a tight portrait.\r\n  618:         ce = char_entry if isinstance(char_entry, dict) else {}\r\n  619:         subject = str(ce.get(\"portrait_prompt\") or ce.get(\"appearance\")\r\n  620:                       or ce.get(\"character_description\") or \"\").strip()\r\n  621:         if not subject:\r\n  622:             subject = \"a period-dressed character, face clearly visible\"\r\n  623:     else:\r\n  624:         subject = get_open_subject(role, synthetic=(kind == \"scene_open\"),\r\n  625:                                    meta=meta, style=_style)\r\n  626:     m = _meta(meta)\r\n  627:     terms = m.get(\"story_brief_terms\") or {}\r\n  628:     if not isinstance(terms, dict):\r\n  629:         terms = {}\r\n  630:     setting = \", \".join([str(t).strip() for t in (terms.get(\"setting\") or [])\r\n  631:                          if str(t).strip()][:2])\r\n  632:     if is_portrait:\r\n  633:         framing = STILL_FRAMING_PORTRAIT\r\n  634:     elif is_char_scene:\r\n  635:         framing = STILL_FRAMING_SCENE_CHARACTER\r\n  636:     elif kind == \"scene_beat\":\r\n  637:         framing = STILL_FRAMING_SCENE_BEAT\r\n  638:     else:\r\n  639:         framing = STILL_FRAMING_OPEN\r\n  640:     pieces = [subject]\r\n  641:     if setting:\r\n  642:         pieces.append(setting)\r\n  643:     pieces.append(framing)\r\n  644:     pieces.append(get_era_tail(meta, profile=\"still\", style=_style))\r\n  645:     pieces.append(_style.positive_tail)\r\n  646:     if not is_portrait:\r\n  647:         # BUG-411: restore the 6/5 cinematic grade + the radio broadcast-distress\r\n  648:         # identity the image-pipeline rewrite dropped. Scene stills are all radio\r\n  649:         # context (open/announcer/music), so both tails apply; appended AFTER the\r\n  650:         # shared style tail and BEFORE the NO_TEXT_CLAUSE so the 5-layer\r\n  651:         # order and the no-text contract are preserved. Portraits are unchanged\r\n  652:         # (they keep their three-quarter framing + the shared style tail).\r\n  653:         # Stage 3: both come from the pack; empty strings vanish in the join.\r\n  654:         pieces.append(_style.image_grade_tail)\r\n  655:         # BUG 1 (2026-06-20): the character SCENE still is NOT a radio booth --\r\n  656:         # it shows the character in their world, so the broadcast-booth tail\r\n  657:         # (\"centered composition\", broadcast-distress) is dropped for this kind.\r\n  658:         # Stage 3: also gated by the pack's allow_radio_tails.\r\n  659:         if not is_char_scene and _style.allow_radio_tails:\r\n  660:             pieces.append(_style.broadcast_tail)\r\n  661:     out = \", \".join(p.strip().rstrip(\",\") for p in pieces if p and p.strip())\r\n  662:     if not is_portrait:\r\n  663:         out = f\"{out}, {NO_TEXT_CLAUSE}\"\r\n  664:     return out\r\n  665: \r\n  666: \r\n  667: def finish_visual_prompt(meta: Any, prompt: str, *, max_chars: int = 0,\r\n  668:                          style_tail: bool = True,\r\n  669:                          era_profile: str = \"full\",\r\n  670:                          style: Any = None) -> str:\r\n  671:     \"\"\"``prompt + \", \" + era_tail [+ \", \" + pack.positive_tail]`` -- the one\r\n  672:     shared finishing seam every visual prompt site calls.\r\n  673: \r\n  674:     Stage 3: the style tail + the era-tail default come from the resolved\r\n  675:     visual-style pack (``style`` param; None => fail-loud\r\n  676:     ``get_visual_style(meta)`` -- this IS a composer entry seam). A\r\n  677:     style-resolution error RAISES; callers must NOT wrap this in a bare\r\n  678:     except (AST-pinned, no-fallback law).\r\n  679: \r\n  680:     ``max_chars`` (0 = uncapped): word-boundary trim of the FINISHED string\r\n  681:     for budgeted consumers (LTX motion budget is 220-240 chars); a trailing\r\n  682:     :data:`NO_TEXT_CLAUSE` present in ``prompt`` survives the trim (it is a\r\n  683:     render constraint, not flavor). Callers run their guards BEFORE this and\r\n  684:     compute prompt hashes AFTER it. Pure; raises ONLY on a visual-style\r\n  685:     resolution failure (fail-loud by design); empty ``prompt``\r\n  686:     returns '' (finishing never invents a subject).\r\n  687: \r\n  688:     ``era_profile`` (LTX-I2V ticket Part A, 2026-06-11): passed through to\r\n  689:     :func:`get_era_tail`. Default ``\"full\"`` = every pre-existing call site,\r\n  690:     byte-identical. The LTX scene composer passes ``\"still\"`` so VIDEO\r\n  691:     prompts share the stills' trimmed palette diet (the full top-3 palette\r\n  692:     tail is what dragged LTX scene clips reddish while the FLUX stills,\r\n  693:     already on the still profile, stayed balanced).\r\n  694:     \"\"\"\r\n  695:     base = (prompt or \"\").strip().rstrip(\",\")\r\n  696:     if not base:\r\n  697:         return \"\"\r\n  698:     _style = _resolve_style(meta, style)\r\n  699:     # Preserve the clause only when TRAILING (pass-02 panel: an occurrence\r\n  700:     # mid-prompt is content, not a render constraint to relocate).\r\n  701:     keep_no_text = base.endswith(NO_TEXT_CLAUSE)\r\n  702:     if keep_no_text:\r\n  703:         base = base[: -len(NO_TEXT_CLAUSE)].strip().rstrip(\",\").strip()\r\n  704:     pieces = [base, get_era_tail(meta, profile=era_profile, style=_style)]\r\n  705:     if style_tail:\r\n  706:         pieces.append(_style.positive_tail)\r\n  707:     out = \", \".join(p for p in pieces if p)\r\n  708:     if max_chars and len(out) > max_chars:\r\n  709:         budget = max_chars - (len(NO_TEXT_CLAUSE) + 2 if keep_no_text else 0)\r\n  710:         cut = out[:max(budget, 20)]\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
