{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"agent_message","text":"VERDICT: no — full-story provenance, bounded generation, exact target consumption, strict artifact shape, canonical wiring, and a meaningful live proof still have build-blocking defects.\n\nMUST-FIX BEFORE BUILD:\n\n1. [§2.5, §4.3–4.4; Lesson 5] P-A may head-truncate accepted story text, contradicting both “reads the final accepted/frozen story” and “NEVER truncates.” Remove truncation: P-A receives the complete line spine or preflight aborts before generation. `kibitz-runs/2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual/r4/input.md:14-17,439-448,601-608`; `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:66-75`.\n\n2. [§4.3–4.4, §10/I2–I3; Lessons 4–5] Budgeting is not implementable. Most authored strings, list cardinalities, evidence counts, and `mood` are unbounded; the repair equation double-counts input/output, while the real repair helper echoes only 400 failed-output characters. Define every bound, requested sampling value, and deterministic source-order batch rule. Preflight `max(base_call_tokens, actual_repair_call_tokens) <= configured_safe_cap`; separately record advertised/native and configured-safe caps, exact versus conservative counting, and fail if cap/count is unknown. Close constrained-generation behavior for both P-A and P-B per provider. `r4/input.md:625-665,1258-1266`; `nodes/_otr_repair_prompts.py:111-152`; `nodes/_otr_model_catalog.py:1200-1269`.\n\n3. [§2.5, §3.2, §7.1; Lessons 1, 5] `DirectionSourceV1` has no unique ledger projection. Production stores `story_brief` as a string, flat palette/key-object fields, and nested `story_brief_terms={setting,lighting,atmosphere}`; the plan instead specifies both `lighting` and an untyped `story_brief_terms`. It also leaves `cast[].traits` string-versus-list normalization ambiguous and misstates `episode_id` as coming from meta instead of the top-level ledger. Define exact source paths, closed types, and normalization; use one canonical representation with no duplicated lighting. `r4/input.md:417-435,502-516`; `nodes/_otr_story_brief.py:841-860`; `nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:454-465`; `nodes/production_ledger.py:551-571`.\n\n4. [§2.2, §4.1, §4.5, §9.1.3; Lessons 2–4, 14] The wrong-depth defense still regressed. P-A’s ownership prose omits top-level `era_cues`, and the “per-pass” test places `era_tail_2` in P-B although P-B has no era field. Create one exact parent/key table for every P-A/P-B object and collection, shared by schema, base prompt, fixture, validator, and repair. Test authoritative-top-level plus nested extras, absent/empty top-level, identical versus conflicting candidates, wrong types, unknown keys, duplicate IDs, full post-validation, and zero LLM calls after successful deterministic repair. `r4/input.md:548-557,697-708,1077-1082`; `docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:469-487`.\n\n5. [§2.2–2.6, §7.6; Lessons 11, 13] Executable fields can evade semantic grounding by selecting `kind=\"rationale\"`; inline motif/clue/shot evidence has no `kind` at all, and `{id,quote}` cannot identify which cast/brief list leaf was cited. Require at least one factual positive anchor for every executable `look.*` field and still-direction row, with closed `field/path`, index where needed, `start`, `end`, and exact-slice `quote`. Persist the normalized source DTO or bounded per-path source receipt so a later mismatch identifies first drift rather than only reporting a whole-object hash. `r4/input.md:297-306,520-527,954-965`; `docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:489-495`; `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:142-153,167-177`.\n\n6. [§2.3–2.4, §5.4, §8.6/8.9] Persisted `style_pack.is_dynamic=true` would fail `_validate_row`, which rejects every non-v2 key. Remove it from the stored payload; add runtime-only `VisualStyle.is_dynamic=False`, set true only after validating a `dynamic_story` payload against the exact v2 schema and path-stem rule. Also pin the safety base key-for-key or identify a hashed authoritative source—its current values are unspecified, 