he vetted talking look, or explicitly define a constrained dynamic cue and revise D6. Separately, preserve `get_story_brief_ltx` as semantic scene content; only its look/palette authority is suppressed. Pass the resolved dynamic style to the finisher instead of deleting the narrative core. `nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_driver.py:619-641,2052-2089`; `nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:618-636`; `nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:149-170`.\n\n10. [§8.3; Lesson 7] The claimed literal workflow delta is not literal: `order` remains a placeholder and output slots 1/2 lack indexes. Specify a valid complete node record—node 96 at order 4, with current orders ≥4 shifted—and reconcile array placement, links, output fan-outs, and widgets. Canonical node 63 currently has no active profile/master stamp, contradicting “no widget change” followed by “master hash stamp”; leave canonical stamps empty, compute its receipt hash, then regenerate and verify all committed stamped variants. `r4/input.md:998-1026`; `workflows/otr_canonical.json:1`; `nodes/_otr_workflow_validator.py:394-408`; `scripts/build_variants.py:129-157,316-338`.\n\n11. [§8.2, §9.1.20; ComfyUI node contract] AST presence in `_NODE_MODULES` does not prove registration: root loading catches import failure and silently omits both mappings. Add a cold package-import test asserting the concrete class and label in `NODE_CLASS_MAPPINGS` and `NODE_DISPLAY_NAME_MAPPINGS`, then pin `INPUT_TYPES`, `FUNCTION`, `CATEGORY`, return names/types, and actual tuple arity. `__init__.py:351-367`; `tests/test_workflow_contract_validation.py:41-98`.\n\n12. [§9.1.8, §9.3; Lessons 7–8] The live control cannot byte-match a committed pre-feature prompt: Writer always re-executes and local generation samples without a seed. Keep byte-identity proof in captured-ledger/injected tests; live control should prove named-pack pass-through, no dynamic receipts, and successful publication. Canonical defaults also select visualizers that ignore stills, so a dynamic smoke can publish without exercising story-directed pixels. Run control/dynamic qualification with the same explicit still-consuming configuration, assert a generated still and artifact-authored prompt clauses, then verify final episode/OBS assets. `r4/input.md:1095-1099,1183-1193`; `nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3034-3038`; `nodes/_otr_model_loader.py:1122-1129`; `nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:398-425,561-566`; `nodes/_otr_video_engines/cheap_families.py:222-240`.\n\n13. [§3, §9.4; Lessons 1, 6, 10] The sprint receipt omits Dispatcher and ShotLock as authoritative durable provenance writers and does not define when `PASS` is legal or whether 720w is required versus `NOT RUN`. Add mechanical PASS criteria and an exact build sequence: capture/commit/push baselines first; land code, consumers, registration, tests, canonical JSON, and variants as one activation chunk; run all gates and push; qualify 30w then 120w; record 720w status explicitly; verify `HEAD==origin`. `r4/input.md:492-516,1203-1225`; `AGENTS.md:73-81,134-142`.\n\nSHOULD-FIX:\n\n1. [§9.2] Record each qualification leg as explicit creative-slot and technical-slot assignments, with concrete provider/model IDs, prompt hashes, constrained mode, cap/count source, and repair counts. The cloud lane must be declared before harness implementation, not merely before execution. `r4/input.md:1165-1179`.\n\n2. [§9.3; Lessons 8–9] Make the operational gate explicit: selective reset, empty port, baseline VRAM, UTF-8 canonical launcher, server and leg logs, watchdog, queue/history/runner verdicts, and one-variable comparisons. A reusable live failure must update both `PROD_BUG_LOG.md` and the relevant preflight/planning guide. `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:110-129`.\n\nOPTIONAL / NICE-TO-HAVE:\n\n1. [§9.1.21] Add a small perceptual-difference metric to the operator look rubric after functional gates; it must not replace prompt/provenance and human visual review.\n\nCUT THESE:\n\n1. [§8.1] Cut unwired `dire